ntrol, and platform automation.<br><br>· Evaluate, customize, and integrate technologies such as OpenBMC and other open-source management frameworks.<br><br>· Enable remote platform access, recovery, and management capabilities for engineering teams.<br><br>· Collaborate with hardware teams on schematic reviews, hardware integration, and bring-up requirements.<br><br>· Create tools, scripts, and automation to improve validation efficiency and engineering productivity.<br><br>· Support first-silicon bring-up, board debugging, and platform validation activities.<br><br>· Debug hardware and firmware interactions using oscilloscopes, logic analyzers, and other laboratory equipment.<br><br>· Support manufacturing test, firmware provisioning, and lifecycle management processes.<br><br>· Drive technical execution across multiple projects while contributing to architecture, risk reduction, and long-term platform strategy.<br><br>· Generate design documentation, validation procedures, and engineering guidelines.<br><br><strong>Minimum Qualifications: </strong><br><br>· Bachelor's or Master's degree in <strong>Electrical Engineering</strong>, <strong>Computer Engineering</strong>, <strong>Embedded Systems</strong>, or a related field.<br><br>· 5+ years of experience developing embedded firmware and software.<br><br>· Strong proficiency in embedded C/C++ development.<br><br>· Solid understanding of digital hardware design and board-level electronics.<br><br>· Experience reading and reviewing schematics, PCB layouts, datasheets, and hardware interface specifications.<br><br>· Familiarity with I2C/SMBus, SPI, UART, GPIO, JTAG, and other common embedded interfaces.<br><br>· Experience debugging embedded systems using oscilloscopes, logic analyzers, and related laboratory equipment.<br><br>· Experience with Linux-based development environments.<br><br>· Strong problem-solving and cross-functional collaboration skills.<br><br><strong>Preferred Qualificacions: </strong><br><br>· Exp