&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/klaviyo/software-engineer-ii-sms-international-london-109336","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1795168514},{"slug":"principal-compliance-officer-london-420603","company_name":"Xai","title":"Principal Compliance Officer","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;SpaceX was founded under the belief that a future where humanity is out exploring the stars is fundamentally more exciting than one where we are not. Today, SpaceX is actively developing the technologies to make this possible, with the ultimate goal of making life multiplanetary and expanding consciousness to the stars.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;SpaceXSI is building Super Intelligence to help humanity understand the universe. Our teams are building the full Super Intelligence stack: from our Colossus supercomputers, to Grok models, to our suite of applications, including Grok Bot, Grok Build, Grok Imagine, Grok Voice, and X. We&#39;re creating a powerful flywheel where more compute trains better models, better models power more useful products, and what we learn from people using those products shapes what we build next.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PRINCIPAL COMPLIANCE OFFICER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The UK financial crime program is being built now, and it has to stand up to the FCA. This role sits in Compliance, reports to the US BSA/AML Officer, and owns the UK framework end to end — AML/CTF, sanctions, fraud, ABC, KYC/CDD/EDD, transaction monitoring, SARs, and the operating rhythm. You will still work the hard cases. It is a builder seat with accountability, not a queue job with “strategy” in the title.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have eight or more years inside an FCA-regulated bank, EMI, PI, or payments firm, have owned or rebuilt a financial crime control framework, and can still open a file, this is the seat. You will build the UK program from the ground up, setting the standards the team and the FCA will use. This is consumer-scale payments financial crime work – not a private-banking book – and you’ll sit directly with Product and Engineering. You’ll operate in a small team with a direct line to the US BSA/AML Officer, where scope is broad and process is lean. The measure of success is a program that still works a year later, and the role sits alongside MLRO / SMF17-adjacent duties for the UK entity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and run the UK financial crime programme: policy, procedures, CDD/EDD, risk rating, sanctions screening, transaction monitoring, SAR handling, escalation, QA, and training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn MLR 2017, POCA, the Sanctions and Anti-Money Laundering Act, JMLSG, the FCA Financial Crime Guide, SYSC 6.3, and payments/EMI expectations into something operations and product can run&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the UK business-wide risk assessment and keep it honest as the product, customer mix, and channels change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle complex cases — PEPs, adverse media, sanctions hits, high-risk onboarding, fraud typologies, escalations — then use the queue to fix the framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stand up first- and second-line controls: documentation, workflows, vendor oversight, quality sampling, MI, and issue management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Put UK requirements into the customer journey with Legal, Operations, Product, and Engineering. Be the UK voice in global design decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on quality, residual risk, throughput, and control health, and prepare the program for internal audit, skilled-person reviews, and FCA scrutiny&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the operating model as the team grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, coach, and set the standard&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support MLRO / SMF17-adjacent duties as the UK permissions model requires&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BASiC QUALIFICATIONS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of hands-on experience with financial crime in a regulated UK firm (bank, EMI, PI, payments, or e-money), including substantial KYC/CDD/EDD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PREFERRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will still do the cases, close gaps in a small team, do not wait for a 30-page RACI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You know the UK regime well enough to argue a point — MLR 2017, JMLSG, POCA, UK sanctions, FCA expectations — and how it lands in a payments product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have designed or rebuilt a framework, procedure, or control, not only cleared files or written a policy nobody ran&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have led people or a workstream. You can defend a risk decision and explain it to the Product without jargon&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU financial crime experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the EU AML package, 6AMLD, EBA guidelines, national transposition, or an EU FIU/regulator, especially on cross-border payments, wallets, or EMI/PI products (useful because X Money will not stay inside one perimeter)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ADDITIONAL REQUIREMENTS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-office five days a week; occasional work-from-home when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive base + equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;UK private medical covering GPs and specialists; pension; life insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days’ paid time off; lunch and dinner allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;SpaceXSI is an equal opportunity employer. For details on data processing, view our&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://x.ai/legal/recruitment-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/xai/principal-compliance-officer-london-420603","tags":["Safety"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1795168514},{"slug":"vp-of-engineering-london-hybrid-247550","company_name":"Clearbank","title":"VP of Engineering","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">We built ClearBank on the belief that banking infrastructure would no longer slow down progress. Instead, it would be a catalyst that unlocks the potential to innovate. It would adapt to different needs so a new era in financial services could begin. We’re here to challenge the status quo in banking, are you?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We all know that transforming banking forever is not an easy mission, but we’re more than ready to rise to that challenge. We all do it every day; navigating new, unexpected and sometimes even daunting challenges. But we believe in ourselves and trust we can do it. Want to innovate? Go for it. Push for a better way? You Can. If you think you have it in you, this is Where You Can.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">ClearBank is a technology‑enabled, fully regulated bank providing cloud‑based banking and payments infrastructure to financial institutions. We operate at scale in a highly regulated environment, where trust, resilience and security are critical.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our engineering organisation is focused on enabling frequent, reliable change while maintaining strong controls. We believe quality is not a gate at the end of delivery, but something designed in from the very start.</p><div style="text-align:left"><img style="max-width:100%" src="data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAMAAAADCAYAAABWKLW/AAAADklEQVR4AWJiQAK4OQAAAAD//3HbuhMAAAAGSURBVAMAAMMAB7vv1tQAAAAASUVORK5CYII=" width="2" height="2" /></div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Role Purpose</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a senior leadership role accountable for the strategy, design, build, operation and ongoing resilience of ClearBank’s payments and cards platforms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The VP of Payments &amp; Cards will lead multiple engineering teams responsible for real-time, scheme-connected payments and cards systems across the UK, Europe, and future international markets. This requires deep experience working close to the infrastructure that moves money. Ideally, this will include direct integration with major payment schemes or rails, such as FPS, Bacs or CHAPS in the UK, SEPA payment schemes in Europe, or ACH and Fedwire in the US. We will also consider experience gained through payment infrastructure providers or connectivity platforms provided it includes sufficient technical depth in payment processing, scheme connectivity and the operation of highly available, regulated payments infrastructure. The role will define platform strategy, engineering standards, tooling and ways of working, while embedding a shift-left quality mindset across delivery. Success means delivering highly resilient, highly available, secure, scalable and compliant platforms that enable frequent, reliable change in a regulated banking environment.</p><div style="text-align:left"><img style="max-width:100%" src="data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAMAAAADCAYAAABWKLW/AAAADklEQVR4AWJiQAK4OQAAAAD//3HbuhMAAAAGSURBVAMAAMMAB7vv1tQAAAAASUVORK5CYII=" width="2" height="2" /></div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Key Responsibilities</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the strategy, design, build and run of real-time payments and cards platforms across the UK, Europe, the US and future international markets, including direct scheme connectivity and integrations with third-party payment infrastructure providers.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the delivery and operation of digital wallet capabilities, including Apple Pay and Google Pay implementations.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the technical direction for payments and cards platforms, ensuring architectural choices support resilience, availability, scalability, performance, security and cost efficiency.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the budget for the Payments and Cards engineering teams, ensuring effective investment in people, tooling and platforms.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build, lead and develop high-performing engineering teams, creating clear accountability, strong delivery discipline and a culture of engineering excellence.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure platforms are designed and operated to meet the following outcomes:</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Highly resilient — supporting local and cross-region disaster recovery requirements.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Highly available — targeting 99.999% aggregate internal availability where appropriate.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Highly scalable — supporting aggressive growth targets and future business volumes.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Performant — meeting scheme performance requirements and exceeding client expectations on latency.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cost optimised — balancing client value, operational efficiency and ClearBank’s cost base.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish scalable engineering quality standards, practices and governance across the payments and cards domain.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Embed quality, observability, operational readiness and control requirements into delivery practices and CI/CD pipelines.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive engineering productivity through AI-assisted and increasingly agentic software engineering, including the effective use of AI coding tools and multi-agent approaches across development, testing and engineering workflows, with appropriate risk, security and regulatory guardrails.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with the CTO, engineering leaders, product, risk, compliance and operations teams to ensure delivery decisions balance pace, quality and control.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure software development and platform operations meet regulatory, audit, resilience and compliance expectations.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Skills &amp; Experience</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Senior engineering leadership experience in payments, cards or highly regulated financial technology environments.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience establishing, scaling and operating engineering teams, standards and practices.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct experience integrating with, building against or operating connectivity to payment schemes or rails. Relevant examples include Faster Payments, Bacs or CHAPS in the UK; SEPA payment schemes and associated euro payment infrastructure in Europe; ACH or Fedwire in the US; or card networks and associated issuing or acquiring infrastructure. Alternatively, substantial experience delivering payment connectivity through a provider such as Form3 or an equivalent platform, with demonstrable technical depth in how payments are processed, routed and operated.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience delivering or operating digital wallet capabilities, such as Apple Pay and Google Pay.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of real-time, high-availability, high-throughput distributed systems.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong background working in regulated environments, with practical experience of audit, compliance, operational resilience and control frameworks.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep understanding of shift-left quality, test automation, modern quality engineering and secure software development practices.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience using modern AI-enabled engineering tooling and a strong understanding of how agentic or multi-agent approaches can improve software development, testing and engineering delivery in a controlled and responsible way.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong security mindset, with an appreciation of evolving threats, mitigations and secure platform design.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated ability to influence across multiple teams and senior stakeholders, including where direct line management is not present.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent collaboration and communication skills, with the ability to work effectively with engineering, product, risk, compliance and executive stakeholders.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sound judgement in balancing delivery pace, customer outcomes, regulatory expectations, operational risk and engineering quality.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A little bit more about us!</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ClearBank is Where You Can belong:</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At ClearBank we think about Diversity, Equity and Inclusion (DE&amp;I) a lot. Not because we think we should. But because we know we should – how else can we build a happy workforce and be successful as a business. We’re committed to making sure our teams reflect society. And we put energy and effort into making this a place where everyone feels at home, where they’re given the trust and encouragement to do their very best work. Here are some of the things we’re most proud of: </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">42% of our senior management roles are held by women </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our enhanced family leave policies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Launching our partnership with Code First Girls </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Increasing awareness of neurodiversity in the workplace through our partnership with the Inclusive Group </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our hiring process and what you can expect:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Application:</strong> a member of our talent acquisition team will review your application against the key requirements for the role and let you know within two weeks whether you’re moving forward to the next stage; </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Screening:</strong> You’ll spend 30-45 minutes speaking to one of our recruiters learning more about the role and ClearBank, and we’ll get it know more about you, your experience and how your skills align with the role (this will be via phone or Teams video call). You can expect to hear back from us within seven days following this meeting (if things are taking longer than expected, we’ll let you know that too); </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First Interview:</strong> You’ll spend one hour with a member of our hiring team focusing on your skills, competencies and your ways of working at the same time we’ll give you time to ask more questions about the role, the team and learn more about the ClearBank culture. This will be via Teams.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Second Interview:</strong> This will be a competency-based interview with one or more members of our team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Final Stage: </strong>You will have a final meeting with the Head of Department. This will be around 45-60 minutes.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Offer:</strong> Congratulations! Get ready to transform banking forever! </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our commitment to you as a candidate:</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We will always try our best to get back to you within seven days of your interview whether you’ve been successful or not and provide you with feedback. Sometimes things take a little longer, so we may not have a decision to share but we will get it touch to let you know we need a little more time.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re unable to provide specific individual feedback at the application or screening stage but know that your application was reviewed and considered carefully.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We wish you the best of luck with your application and maybe we’ll be celebrating your new role at ClearBank soon!  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equal Opportunities</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">ClearBank is committed to ensuring equal opportunities throughout every stage of the recruitment process. ClearBank recognises that diversity is vital to the long-term success of the business in the communities and markets in which it operates. ClearBank is also a firm believer that an inclusive culture fosters greater employee engagement and collaboration. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">ClearBank strives for diversity and inclusion of all forms, including (but not limited to): gender, age, educational and professional background, disability, gender reassignment, marital or civil partner status, pregnancy or maternity, race, colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin, religion or belief and sexual orientation. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As part of the Company’s commitment to equal employment opportunity, we provide reasonable adjustments, to candidates during the recruitment process, including to individuals with disabilities. We want to create a safe space that welcomes everyone so please let us know how we can accommodate you. In case you have any accessibility requirements you can share that with our Talent Acquisition team prior to your interview stage, if applicable. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The legal bit</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">By submitting your CV to ClearBank Limited you are providing your consent for us to use the information you provide for recruitment purposes. For more information on how we manage your data go and check out our Candidate Privacy Notice on the ClearBank website to see how we process, manage and look after your data. You are also allowing us to communicate with you by email and telephone for recruitment purposes. </p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/clearbank/vp-of-engineering-london-hybrid-247550","tags":["ClearBank Group Holdings"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London Office - Hybrid","created_at":1795167613},{"slug":"senior-product-manager-data-foundry-london-384299","company_name":"Beamery","title":"Senior Product Manager, Data Foundry","description":"<h3><strong>ABOUT BEAMERY</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">With the rapid expansion of AI and automation, the future of work has never been more challenging for organizations. Beamery’s unique jobs, skills and tasks data platform helps organizations navigate these challenges and make more informed decisions across Talent Lifecycle Management. Our solutions power recruitment, mobility, upskilling, diversity, work architecture and workforce planning for some of the world’s most forward-thinking companies.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe that where you work is much more than just a job. Millions of people are being left behind every day in their careers, and we’re on a mission to fix this by creating equal access to meaningful work, skills and careers for all.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are an equal opportunity employer committed to building a representative Beamery, creating an equitable, inclusive and engaging environment for our people.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">So, what are you waiting for? Join us and help us transform the future of work once and for all.<br /><br /><strong>What’s ahead — and why it’s an exciting time to join the team: </strong><br /><br />Building agentic AI with advanced orchestration (multi-agent workflows, tool use, evaluation loops) that turns complex talent data into decisions.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Training and fine-tuning our own models on unique data about jobs, skills and tasks, and benchmarking them against the best in our market.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Joining an award-winning AI team (ACM RecSys Challenge 2026) that turns new ideas into innovative solutions with scientific rigour.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sharing our work and learning from industry peers through challenges, conferences and publications.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">But it’s not all about creating high-quality products, we also very much value the company culture we have worked hard to create; built on trust, empathy &amp; honesty ensuring our workforce is able to bring their full selves to work.</p><h1>About the opportunity at Beamery</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for an experienced Senior Product Manager to own Beamery's Data Foundry end to end. The Data Foundry is our proprietary data platform, powering existing and emerging product lines including our Talent CRM and Workforce Suite. Through this, we provide data-as-a-service to customers through channels such as MCP/API. This is an emerging commercial channel. Its core capabilities span the data models, taxonomies and integrations that underpin talent and workforce decisions across our platform.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Senior Product Manager, Data Foundry will treat data both as infrastructure embedded within our products and as a product that customers buy in its own right. Beyond internal embedding and direct commercial sales, the platform is open — customers and partners can build on top of it through MCP and API access. You will work with product leadership to set the strategy, agree what the platform provides internally, decide what becomes customer-facing, and define how the platform opens up for customer and partner innovation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will work at the centre of the platform, creating a balance between two essential initiatives. On one side, you serve the Talent CRM and Workforce Suite product managers as your customers, agreeing the data contracts they build on. On the other, you partner with the data science, data engineering and integrations engineering leads to turn those needs into delivery.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>What you will be doing</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><u>Ownership and strategy</u></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the Data Foundry vision, strategy and roadmap, framing each item as a bet with a clear driver, aligned to overall strategic objectives</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure alignment of Data Foundry strategy to Beamery's AI strategy, reflecting the shift from providing AI assistants to providing AI access through MCP and API channels.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Decide what Data Foundry provides as internal infrastructure and what is packaged and sold as a customer-facing product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make and defend build versus buy decisions across integrations, analytics, AI and taxonomy capabilities.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><u>Discovery and commercial impact</u></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Discover and validate what external customers want from data-as-a-service, and partner with Sales and Customer Success to drive adoption with clear GTM and enablement plans</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the case for Data Foundry as a new commercial channel, defining and proving the standalone commercial model alongside its role as platform foundation, quantify the value it unlocks for specific customers and deals, and measure success against value and usage metrics.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><u>Partnership and delivery</u></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead your team to deliver solutions our customers can’t imagine working without and that deliver measurable customer and business outcomes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Agree and maintain the data contracts with the CRM and Workforce Suite product managers, treating them as internal customers with real commitments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prioritise across data science, data engineering and integrations engineering, translating tribe needs into a clear and deliverable plan.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><u>Communication &amp; alignment</u></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate transparently and create alignment between peers and leadership on priorities, trade offs and progress</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage customer and sales expectations through well managed structured cadences</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><u>Data governance and trust</u></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own how workforce data is governed, secured and access-controlled as it is exposed through APIs and MCP, meeting or exceeding enterprise privacy and compliance expectations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure the outputs of Data Foundry's models are measurable and explainable, so customers and internal teams can trust and act on the results.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>What we are looking for</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A product manager with a minimum 6 years experience in complex technical, data or AI products, a significant portion of which should be in enterprise B2B SaaS.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong grasp of data platforms, APIs and integrations, comfortable making architecture-adjacent decisions while collaborating with and holding priorities with engineering and data science leads.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience handling sensitive or regulated data, with a clear view of governance, security and privacy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An analytical thinker who uses data to find opportunities, confidently prioritise and measure success, balancing between competing tribe roadmaps and internal customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercially fluent, experience with 0-1 product stages, shaping early product with new go to market motions, able to connect product decisions to revenue, cost and customer ROI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A clear communicator who builds trust across product, data science and engineering, and who is comfortable taking a position and explaining the reasoning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experienced owning and delivering AI capabilities, with a keen interest in how AI is reshaping the talent and workforce space, and in giving customers trusted, explainable access to their data.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Beamery is for Everybody. Diversity and open expression are fundamental to us. We acknowledge the challenges in our industry and strive to develop an inclusive culture where everybody can contribute. We are dedicated to creating an inclusive environment for everyone, regardless of ethnicity, religion, color, sexual orientation, gender identity, race, national origin, age, disability status, or caregiver status. If, for whatever reason, you need us to make reasonable adjustments and adaptations to our recruitment process, please email </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="c-link" ---------- style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Visit our </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://careers.beamery.com/life-at-beamery/diversity-equality-inclusion/"><em>Diversity, Equality and Inclusion page </em></a><em>to learn more about progress and commitments.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/beamery/senior-product-manager-data-foundry-london-384299","tags":["Product and Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London, UK","created_at":1795167612},{"slug":"chief-medical-officer-uk-i-emea-united-kingdom-162259","company_name":"Lyrebird Health","title":"Chief Medical Officer, UK/I & EMEA","description":"<h2><strong>Chief Medical Officer, UK/I &amp; EMEA</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lyrebird is reshaping how clinical documentation happens across the NHS and in Ireland, and we’re looking for a Chief Medical Officer to be the senior clinical voice of the business. Reporting to the CEO, you’ll make sure everything we build, deploy and sell is clinically safe, evidence-based and genuinely useful to clinicians and patients. You’ll own our clinical safety and governance framework, including DCB0129 and oversight of the Clinical Safety Officer function. You’ll shape the product roadmap alongside Product and Engineering, build the evidence base that NHS and HSE buyers need, and act as a trusted peer to CCIOs, CMIOs, medical directors and ICB leaders.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role suits a practising or recently practising doctor who has led at a senior level in the NHS and knows digital health from the inside. You’re comfortable moving between a board presentation, a hazard log and a conversation with engineers in the same afternoon. You’ll enjoy the pace of a high-growth company, but you’ll never trade safety for speed. You believe clinical AI should be held to the same standards as the rest of medicine, and you want to be the person who proves it can be.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About Us</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lyrebird Health is transforming the quality and accessibility of healthcare by automating clinicians’ most time-consuming tasks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Thousands of clinicians across multiple disciplines use Lyrebird every day in environments where accuracy, safety, and time matter deeply. In the UK, that includes NHS trusts across Cheshire and Merseyside, Alder Hey Children’s, and the South West London Acute Provider Collaborative, one of the largest ambient AI deployments in the country. Everything we build is grounded in earning trust, reducing cognitive load, and delivering meaningful impact at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll do</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead Lyrebird’s clinical safety management system for the UK and Ireland, ensuring DCB0129 compliance, supporting customers with DCB0160, and providing senior oversight of our Clinical Safety Officers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring the clinical voice into the product roadmap, defining UK- and Ireland-specific workflows and leading clinical validation of new models, features and specialty templates before release.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own clinical incident management and chair our clinical governance and safety committee, reporting to the leadership team and board.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advise on the regulatory landscape, including MHRA medical device regulation, NHS England guidance on ambient voice technology, DTAC, and the EU AI Act for Ireland.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and deliver a clinical evidence strategy, running evaluations and real-world studies with NHS and academic partners, publishing the results, and always reporting limitations honestly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a trusted clinical peer to CCIOs, CMIOs, medical directors and digital leaders across NHS trusts, ICBs and the HSE, and represent Lyrebird at conferences, in the media and in national policy conversations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring clinical credibility to the commercial team by leading the clinical, safety and evidence sections of tenders, supporting pilots, and making sure every clinical claim we make stands up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and lead a UK and Ireland clinical team, and champion equity, patient safety and inclusive design across languages, accents and patient groups.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll bring</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full GMC registration with a licence to practise, in good standing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Significant senior clinical leadership experience in the NHS, such as Medical Director, Deputy or Associate Medical Director, or Clinical Director.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Substantial digital health or clinical informatics leadership, for example as a CCIO, CMIO or senior clinical lead on an EPR or digital transformation programme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">In-depth, practical knowledge of DCB0129 and DCB0160, clinical risk management, hazard logs and safety cases, plus a solid grasp of MHRA, DTAC, DSPT and NHS England AI guidance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of designing, leading or publishing clinical evaluations, audits or research.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong NHS networks and the ability to explain complex clinical, technical and regulatory issues clearly to boards, clinicians, engineers and patients.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Nice to have</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Accredited Clinical Safety Officer training, and continuing clinical practice alongside the role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a health tech, MedTech or digital health company, ideally including evaluation of AI or NLP safety and performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of the EU AI Act, EU MDR and the Irish health system, or registration with the Medical Council of Ireland.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Membership or fellowship of the Faculty of Clinical Informatics, or a national profile through the Royal Colleges, NHS England or a Health Innovation Network.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with clinical coding (SNOMED CT, ICD-10, OPCS-4), PRSB standards or the NICE Evidence Standards Framework.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every minute a clinician spends on documentation is a minute taken from their patients. In this role, you’ll help decide how ambient AI is safely adopted across the NHS and in Ireland, setting the standards that protect patients while giving clinicians time back to focus on care.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re building a team that reflects the diversity of the people who benefit from our work. We want Lyrebird to be a place where everyone feels safe, supported, and able to thrive. If you’re from an underrepresented background in tech, we strongly encourage you to apply, even if you don’t meet every requirement.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/lyrebird-health/chief-medical-officer-uk-i-emea-united-kingdom-162259","tags":["Clinical"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom","created_at":1795167611},{"slug":"lead-product-manager-london-474316","company_name":"Trading212","title":"Lead Product Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Our mission is to enable everyone to build wealth</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We reinvent how trading and investing work by creating exceptional products people love. Fostering a culture of excellence and high velocity is the key to our success. Тoday, we serve over 6 million clients, with more than €38 billion in assets under management — a testament to the scale and trust we’ve built in just a few years.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>The role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll lead several related product areas, or one of unusual regulator