o the US market, a significant step in our ambition to become a truly global exchange. Joining now means being part of that next chapter, not just maintaining what's already built.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At the heart of our success are our people. We create a high-performance environment where exceptional talent can thrive, blending deep business experience with a commercial mindset to drive strategic growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Team</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Finance makes sure Smarkets has accurate, timely numbers to run the business, satisfy regulators, and stand up to investor scrutiny — across multiple jurisdictions and licences. Two things keep us busy:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reporting &amp; Control</strong> — close, statutory accounts, audit, and the controls framework behind a dual UKGC/CFTC regulated business</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Systems &amp; Transformation</strong> — building out reporting on top of our ERP and automating away the manual stuff</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">A typical week: run a clean close and turn it into a board-ready pack, write a technical paper on a tricky accounting area, ship an automated process and make it audit-ready.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Role:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a detail-oriented, proactive GL Accountant to take ownership of our core accounting operations and general ledger. In this role, you will play a key part in driving the accuracy of our monthly close, ensuring robust balance sheet integrity, and delivering clear financial reporting for internal and external stakeholders.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an operational accounting role where you will own the integrity of the General Ledger end-to-end: keeping ledgers accurate, resolving complex accounting issues, and ensuring audit readiness.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you will do:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own and maintain the General Ledger (GL), ensuring all financial transactions are accurately recorded and mapped</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Execute the month-end close (m/e) process efficiently and accurately to tight timelines</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Perform comprehensive balance sheet and account reconciliations, identifying and resolving any variances</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare and process VAT, tax returns and payroll</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare monthly management accounts and deliver insightful variance analysis</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assist with cash flow forecasting</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the preparation of year-end financial statements and liaise with external auditors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a key liaison to investigate and resolve departmental accounting issues across the business</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assist in driving internal control improvements and supporting automation within our AI-driven ERP environment</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Role Requirements:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Part-qualified or newly qualified ACCA/ACA/CIMA, with a strong foundation in core accounting principles</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven hands-on experience in general ledger management and month-end close processes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong technical skills in balance sheet reconciliations, journal entries, and financial controls</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working in a fast-moving finance team with high standards of data accuracy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication and problem-solving skills, capable of resolving cross-departmental queries</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with ERP systems and process automation tools is a plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a regulated industry (betting, gaming, financial services, or similar) is a plus</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Values</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our values are at the heart of everything we do - guiding how we work, collaborate, and innovate. They reflect what we expect of ourselves and each other to deliver the best results, while fostering a positive, high-performing environment:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Push to Win:</strong> We set ambitious goals and relentlessly pursue them, always striving for excellence.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make Others Better:</strong> We lift each other up, share knowledge, and celebrate team success over individual achievement.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Give a Shit:</strong> We care deeply about our work, our users, and the impact we make.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be a Pro:</strong> We take ownership, act with integrity, and consistently deliver to a high standard.<br /></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring the Energy:</strong> We bring positivity, curiosity, and enthusiasm to everything we do, inspiring those around us.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Culture Fit:</strong> These values define how we succeed as a team. If this <em>isn’t</em> you, this may not be the right place. We hire people who thrive in a fast-paced, collaborative, and ambitious environment.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Perks &amp; Benefits</strong><br />We offer a competitive salary and benefits package, alongside a dynamic, collaborative environment where your work truly makes an impact and your voice is heard. Our team is diverse, driven, and ambitious - united by a strong work ethic and a hunger to innovate and win.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our benefits are designed around Health, Wealth,and Development, supporting you both professionally and personally.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">These include:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stock Options:</strong> Vest over 4 years - your success is our success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pension Scheme:</strong> Competitive plan via Aviva, with up to 6% matched contributions if you opt in.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Health Insurance:</strong> Comprehensive coverage to keep you and your family healthy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enhanced Parental Leave:</strong> Enhanced maternity and paternity leave to support you through life’s most important moments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stay Fuelled:</strong> Enjoy fresh, chef-made breakfast and lunch every day, plus a constant supply of fruit, snacks, tea, coffee and soft drinks — because great work starts with great food.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cycle-to-Work Scheme:</strong> Support for sustainable commuting and staying active.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning &amp; Development:</strong> £1,000 annual education budget for courses, conferences, books, or training.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Holiday:</strong> 25 days paid leave + bank holidays, with the option to carry over 5 days.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexible Working:</strong> Hybrid model with 3 days in the office and 2 days from home to fit your lifestyle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team Energy:</strong> Regular socials, hackathons, and events — because collaboration and fun go hand-in-hand.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What happens next​</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We aim to have a simple and speedy hiring process, and we want to make sure we're right for you as much as the other way around.</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Initial screening</strong> — a quick chat with our recruiter about your experience and the role</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience &amp; mindset interview</strong> — a conversation about your background and what drives you</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competency interview</strong> — with the hiring manager and team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lunch &amp; leadership team</strong> — lunch with the wider team, plus time with members of our leadership team</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Diversity &amp; Inclusion</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re an equal opportunities employer and celebrate diversity in all its forms. If you need any adjustments during the recruitment process, please let us know — we’re happy to accommodate your needs.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/smarkets/general-ledger-gl-accountant-london-314737","tags":["Finance"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1795167611},{"slug":"sales-operations-lead-london-40625","company_name":"Watershed","title":"Sales Operations Lead","description":"<h2>About Watershed</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://watershed.com/">Watershed</a> is the enterprise sustainability platform. Companies like Airbnb, Carlyle Group, FedEx, Visa, and Dr. Martens use Watershed to manage climate and ESG data, produce audit-ready metrics for voluntary and regulatory reporting including CSRD, and drive real decarbonization. We are looking for team members who love product-building, want to work hard at a mission-oriented startup, and will collaborate with us in shaping the culture of a growing team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have offices in San Francisco, New York, Denver, London, Paris, Berlin, Sydney, Mexico City, and remote team members across the US and Europe. We hope that you'll be interested in joining us!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Watershed is on a mission to help companies measure, reduce, and report their emissions. Our go-to-market organization continues to grow, with an emphasis on scale and deepening our presence in EMEA. We're looking for a hands-on operator to run sales operations for the region and build the tools &amp; processes our sellers rely on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll partner closely with EMEA sales leadership to drive the day-to-day operating rhythm of the team - forecasting, pipeline reviews, and planning - and dig into the data to identify risks and opportunities for growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a role for an operator who builds what they design and has already rewired their work around AI. Alongside the operating rhythm, your project work will be building AI agents, tools, and workflows that help our AEs, SDRs, and Solutions teams move our revenue metrics.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This position is based in our London office 4 days per week.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You will:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with EMEA sales leaders to shape and execute our growth strategy in the region</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support headcount, territory, and quota planning for the region, including account ownership and territory governance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the EMEA forecasting process: run regular forecast and pipeline reviews, and inspect deals to improve predictability</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and track the metrics that show how our revenue teams are performing, and turn them into clear recommendations for leadership</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be the go-to resource for our London office on Salesforce and our revenue tech stack</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build AI-first workflows and internal tools, with tools like Claude Code, that change how our sales teams work day to day</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You have:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">6+ years of work experience, including 3+ years in Sales Operations, Revenue Operations, or GTM Operations at a high-growth B2B technology company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct experience supporting sales teams: you've run a forecast cadence, territory or quota planning, and the reporting behind a revenue number</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical skills, with hands-on experience building models and interpreting sales metrics</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with Salesforce: you build your own reports and dashboards. Bonus if you've owned administration, automation, or data model design</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is already embedded in how you work. You've built AI workflows that other people use, not just prototypes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communication skills: you turn data into clear recommendations for sales leadership and build trust across teams</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">   </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">   </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Must be willing to work from an office 4 days per week (except for remote roles)</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Watershed has hub offices in San Francisco, New York, London, and Mexico City and satellite offices in Denver, Sydney, Paris, and Berlin. Where we have offices, employees are expected to be in office for 4 days per week. Certain jobs are open to being remote and will be specifically noted on the jobs page and in the job description if so.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What’s the interview process like?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It starts the same for every candidate: getting to know the team members through 1 to 2 conversations about Watershed, your experience, and your interests. Next steps can vary by role, but usual next steps are a skill or experience interview (e.g. a coding interview for an engineer, a portfolio review for a designer, deeper experience call for other roles) which leads to a virtual or in person interview panel. We prioritize transparency and lack of surprise throughout the process.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What if I need accommodations for my interview?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Watershed, we are dedicated to ensuring an inclusive recruitment process. We provide reasonable accommodations for candidates with disabilities, long-term conditions, mental health needs, religious observances, neurodivergence, or pregnancy-related support requirements. If you need assistance during your process, please contact your recruiter.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/watershed/sales-operations-lead-london-40625","tags":["Revenue"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1795167611},{"slug":"senior-people-partner-aldgate-249073","company_name":"Cloudscaler","title":"Senior People Partner","description":"<h1>Senior People Partner</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cloudscaler | London | People Team | Reports to the Chief People Officer | £55,000–£75,000</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Someone has to own the People initiative that doesn’t fit neatly into anyone’s week and the case nobody else should be handling. That someone is you — not as an escalation point, but as the person who runs the day-to-day of this function.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>THE MOMENT</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cloudscaler is 130 people today. We’ll be 170 by the end of this year, and roughly double again in 2027. The People function is being built in real time alongside that growth, rather than inherited from someone who left years ago.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll be the first hire into the People team. For roughly your first year you’ll be the only People professional alongside the CPO, which means running the whole day-to-day of the function: the hardest casework and initiatives, and the operational core that keeps everything moving. A People Partner is planned to join later in 2027, and at that point the operational administration moves to them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is also a role built with room to grow. As the team expands beyond that second hire, we expect this role to take on day-to-day operational leadership of the People Partner practice, but that isn’t the shape of it on day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>WHAT MAKES THIS DIFFERENT</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">In most People teams, the senior generalist is just a People Partner with a harder case queue. Here, the difference is ownership, not just difficulty.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Complex casework:</strong> Rather than simply handling harder cases, you’ll own the most complex cases end to end, with no hand back.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>People initiatives:</strong> Rather than contributing to initiatives someone else drives, you’ll own them from design through to embedding.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Decision-making:</strong> Rather than escalating ambiguity upward, you’ll make the sensible call and document your reasoning.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>CPO partnership:</strong> Rather than acting in a support role to the CPO, you’ll be an operational partner they can confidently delegate to.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>To be clear about the level:</strong> The CPO still designs the People strategy and the systems architecture. You own how it runs day to day, and you’re trusted to run a whole initiative, not just a case. That is a different job to People Partner, not a bigger version of the same one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>THE ROLE</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll sit in the People team reporting to the Chief People Officer. Three strands make up the job:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Casework:</strong> The employee relations situations with the most complexity or sensitivity land with you, start to finish.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Initiatives:</strong> When the CPO needs a piece of work owned (a policy rollout, a wellbeing programme, a piece of the reward or benefits agenda), you take it from design through to something that runs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Operations:</strong> Until the People Partner joins, you’ll own payroll and benefits administration, onboarding, screening and security clearances, and keeping Rippling accurate.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">When the People Partner joins, they’ll report to the CPO. You won’t manage them formally, but you’ll lead their handover, you’ll be the person they come to first, and your judgement will set the standard for how this function operates day to day.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>WHERE THE ROLE STARTS AND STOPS</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">New roles get vague, so here is the boundary as we see it today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Yours</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The most complex and sensitive employee relations casework, end to end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full ownership of People initiatives, from design to embedding.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Acting as the CPO’s operational partner on ambiguous or cross-cutting problems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Until the People Partner joins (planned for later in 2027):</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Payroll and benefits administration, including the monthly payroll cycle in Rippling and Mintago.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pre-onboarding, onboarding and probation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background screening in Zinc.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Security clearance coordination.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rippling data quality, workflows and reporting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our working groups and committees.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Once the People Partner joins:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A structured handover of the operational core.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Day-to-day guidance for the People Partner.</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shared</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ashby, which Talent Acquisition owns. You’ll work in it from offer through to start date on every hire until the People Partner joins, and on senior hires after that.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mentoring and supporting the People Partner on their casework and initiatives, once they join.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Not yours</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruitment delivery, which sits with Talent Acquisition.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The design of the People strategy, the operating model and the systems architecture, which sit with the CPO.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Formal line management of the People Partner, who will report to the CPO.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>THE STACK</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Rippling:</strong> Our single source of truth. Until the People Partner joins you’ll run it day to day, including the monthly payroll cycle, data quality and workflows, and you’ll use its reporting at a level that supports whole initiatives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Zinc:</strong> Background screening. You’ll run checks for every new joiner until the People Partner joins, and stay close to the senior and sensitive hires after that.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ashby:</strong> Owned by Talent Acquisition. You’ll work in it from offer through to start date on the hires you’re responsible for.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Claude:</strong> A daily tool here. You’ll use it for casework preparation, drafting policy and communications, and pulling together the analysis behind an initiative.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mintago:</strong> Our employee benefits and financial wellbeing platform (pensions, salary sacrifice and financial advice). You’ll administer it and keep enrolment accurate until the People Partner takes it on.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>WHAT YOU’LL DO</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the hardest casework.</strong> You’ll run our most complex and sensitive employee relations cases end to end, with the CPO there to sense-check rather than take over.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own initiatives, not tasks.</strong> You’ll take a People initiative from a rough brief to something that’s running and embedded, rather than handing it back once the interesting part is done.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run the operational core.</strong> Until the People Partner joins, you’ll own the monthly payroll cycle in Rippling, benefits administration including Mintago, onboarding, background screening and security clearances. Accurate, on time, and documented as you go.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hand it over well.</strong> When the People Partner arrives, you’ll give them a working system and a clear handover, then stay the person they come to first and the judgement others in the function measure themselves against.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner with senior leaders.</strong> You’ll be credible with leaders on the most difficult conversations: complex change, capability, and situations without a clean playbook.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Use AI properly.</strong> You’ll use Claude daily to take time out of your own week, checking anything that touches a decision about a person and owning the outcome.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Improve what you find.</strong> You’ll spot the gaps in policy, process or practice before anyone else does, and bring the CPO a considered view on the fix, not just the problem.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>WHAT SUCCESS LOOKS LIKE AT 12 MONTHS</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re running the most complex ER cases with confidence, and the CPO isn’t being pulled into them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least one or two People initiatives have gone from a rough brief to something genuinely embedded, owned by you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Payroll, benefits, onboarding and clearances run accurately and on time, and every process is documented well enough to hand over.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ve helped shape the People Partner hire, so the handover is ready when they land.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Senior leaders treat you as a credible operational partner, not an escalation point.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ve made and documented sensible calls in genuinely ambiguous situations, and they’ve held up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The CPO can hand you an ambiguous problem and trust it gets shaped properly.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>WHO WE’RE LOOKING FOR</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deep employee relations experience.</strong> You’ve run complex disciplinaries, grievances and change situations yourself, and you know exactly when to escalate and when not to. CIPD qualification, or solid progress towards it, is welcome.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A track record of owning initiatives.</strong> You can point to work you took from a brief to something that actually ran, not just a project you contributed to.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hands-on with the operational detail.</strong> You’ve owned or closely supported a payroll cycle, benefits administration and onboarding, and you’re comfortable being accountable for their accuracy while also carrying the senior work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Credible with senior leaders.</strong> You can hold your own in a difficult conversation with someone under real pressure and be listened to.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Comfortable operating near-autonomously.</strong> You don’t need a playbook for everything. You make a sensible call, write it down, and check it with the CPO afterwards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ready to grow into people leadership.</strong> You won’t formally manage anyone at the start, but you’ll induct and guide the People Partner when they join, and you should want to lead a team as the structure catches up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Discreet and organised at volume.</strong> Complex casework and live initiatives, often at the same time. You’ll need a system, and it can’t be your memory.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>THE HONEST PART</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role sits in an odd space for now: senior in scope and judgement, without a team underneath it yet. Until the People Partner joins later in 2027, you’ll also be the whole operational team, so a payroll deadline and a complex grievance can land in the same week. That eases as the function grows, but it means the authority you carry day to day has to come from the quality of your work, not a job title.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are not designing the People strategy or the systems architecture. The CPO does that. What you get instead is real ownership of the hardest cases and the initiatives that matter, a close working relationship with the CPO, and a genuine path toward leading the People Partner practice as it grows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This probably isn’t for you if you want a formal team from day one, or if you’d rather leave payroll and onboarding to someone else. It probably is for you if you want to prove you can run this function well enough, top to bottom, that a team gets built around you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>If that sounds like the challenge you’ve been looking for, let’s talk.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Cloudscaler are proud to be an equal opportunity employer, committed to equal opportunities regardless of gender identity, sexual orientation, race, ancestry, age, marital status, disability, parental status, religion or medical history.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>If you require reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process