&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you are based in California, we encourage you to read this important information for California residents linked &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.suvoda.com/california-applicant-privacy-notice-and-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/suvoda/senior-product-manager-146874","tags":["Product Management"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1795157716},{"slug":"people-performance-manager-united-kingdom-246305","company_name":"tem","title":"People Performance Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>📈 Who We Are:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We are rebuilding the energy transaction, making it transparent and fair.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're rebuilding how energy is bought and sold. That means cutting out middlemen, connecting businesses directly with renewable generators, and ensuring every transaction is <strong>traceable and transparent</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're a <strong>160+ person</strong> team - operators, data scientists, engineers, customer champions and energy experts - backed by top-tier investors including Lightspeed Venture Partners, Hitachi Ventures, Allianz, AlbionVC and Atomico. We closed a <strong>$75M Series B</strong> round in early 2026, taking our total funding to $94M, and we now power energy for over <strong>4,000 UK businesses</strong> across <strong>8,500+ sites</strong>, <strong>with over £75m</strong> in value returned to businesses and generators so far.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're a technology company solving the energy industry, not an energy company. Some people call us a neo-utility, the neo-bank idea, applied to energy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The industry is noticing. We were crowned <strong>Europe's Most Exciting Tech Company</strong> at the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.gpbullhound.com/articles/allstars-awards-2026-winners-announced/">GP Bullhound Allstars awards</a>, came in at <strong>#6</strong> on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/linkedin-top-startups-2026-20-uk-companies-rise-linkedin-news-uk-xoffc">LinkedIn's Top Startups 2026</a> in the UK, <strong>#7</strong> on the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://scalingeurope.co.uk/">Scaling Europe 50</a> of Europe's fastest-growing companies, and <strong>#14</strong> on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://lnkd.in/p/ehxWgJyc">Sifted's AI 100</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learn more about us on our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.tem.energy/">website</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>🚀 The Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're hiring a People Performance Manager to join our Performance Service.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">tem is growing fast. Our goal is to get better as we get bigger - revenue growing faster than headcount. In practice that means keeping our strongest people engaged and performing, getting new joiners productive quickly, and enabling our leaders to multiply their impact over time. Most companies solve that with layers of management. We don't. Our leaders (Player-Coaches) coach their teams while staying hands-on with the work, which means the systems around them have to do more of the lifting. That's where the Performance Service comes in.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're a team of four, and we own how tem runs as an organisation: the operating rhythm (how work gets planned, tracked, escalated and reported), the onboarding and development that build capability, the frameworks that define what good performance looks like and how people progress and get paid, and the operational backbone of contracts, benefits and payroll. We don't own recruitment. We're adding a second Performance Partner because we need more hands on deck - both partnering with our leaders day to day, and building the frameworks that support them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your patch is sustained performance - the part that runs continuously once someone is through the door. You'll carry a portfolio of leaders across our Engines and Services that you're accountable for, and you'll co-own the frameworks that sit underneath them alongside the rest of the team. You will not be handed a finished playbook to administer. You'll report into the Performance Service Manager. HR experience is welcome but not required - we're open to operators, people who've led teams, and the sort of person who ends up owning whatever the company needs next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In your first 12 months, you might:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Become the first call for a portfolio of leaders on anything to do with their people - performance calls, team decisions and hard conversations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Co-design how progression, performance standards, evaluation and reward actually work at tem, alongside the rest of the Performance team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Handle live cases end to end - performance management, difficult conversations, exits and restructures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use AI and automation so the operational layer runs itself and your time goes on judgement, not process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn recurring employee and manager pain points into better processes, tools, guidance or self-service, and measure whether they work.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>🛠️ Responsibilities</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Coach and challenge:</strong> be a leader's first call on anything to do with their people - a decision they want a second view on, coaching on how to handle a situation, or a read on employment law - and hold a position when you disagree with them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Raise the bar:</strong> hold leaders to a high standard on performance, potential, pay and progression - help them make sharper calls, and hold consistency across your patch.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Handle live cases end to end:</strong> performance management, difficult conversations, exits and restructures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build to delight:</strong> shape how progression, performance standards, evaluation and reward actually work at tem, alongside the rest of the Performance team. We treat our people like top athletes, and our aim is to delight them at every step of their employee experience - the systems around them have to express that at every contact point.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Design for our shape, not the textbook:</strong> we index on outcomes and impact in everything - how progression works, how teams are structured, what leaders spend their time on. Most standard people frameworks assume a management hierarchy we don't have.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Automate the repeatable:</strong> use AI and automation so the operational layer runs itself and your time goes on judgement, not process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Think in process, scalability and iteration:</strong> turn recurring employee and manager pain points into better processes, tools, guidance or self-service. Measure whether they work and redesign when they don't fit the purpose.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>✅ Requirements</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You do not need a CIPD qualification, and you do not need to have worked in a large, established HR function. You might have been a founder's associate or Chief of Staff at a Series A or B startup, holding the place together while it scaled. You might have built a People function from scratch and taken it from a one-person band to a well-oiled machine. You might have run a team or an Operations function where the people calls were effectively yours, even if People or HR never appeared in your job title. Or you might have done a different job that helped you build the skills below. A background in HR might help you do this job well, but it is not a requirement.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Must-Haves</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've held real accountability for decisions on people - you've partnered with leaders, or managed a team yourself, where hiring, performance and exit calls were either yours or made on your guidance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can be trusted with the hardest conversations in the business and you're recognised for how you handle them, and you understand how decisions about people shape culture and employer brand - balancing efficiency with empathy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've worked in or towards building a high-performance culture, and you're a confident challenger who carries conviction and can influence leadership decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're comfortable operating without a playbook, in a company where the requirements and the shape of your role change constantly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You think from first principles, get to the root cause of complex problems, weigh competing considerations and anticipate second-order consequences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're fluent with Notion, automation and AI tooling - your instinct is to build the thing rather than do it manually a second time - and you write clearly enough that a busy person reads it once and comes away with a clear idea of the situation and the next actions.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Desirable</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employment relations experience in the UK, Europe or the US - we operate across the UK and Europe today, with plans to expand to the US soon.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working across multiple countries, including employer of record arrangements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compensation and benchmarking experience - salary banding, pay review cycles, market data.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>🎁 Benefits &amp; Perks</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stock options so everyone has ownership in our mission.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 days holiday plus public holidays. Swap public holidays for the ones that matter most to you, and enjoy your birthday off.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Remote first and flexible working, with clear core hours and no internal meetings on Friday afternoons.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Up to GBP1,200 or EUR1,400 per year for your remote setup.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Up to GBP150 or EUR170 per month for wellbeing.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>🤝 Interview Process</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We move fast. Most processes take 2 to 3 weeks from first chat to offer. If you need us to adapt anything, let us know.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Intro call with our Talent team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Skills interview, which might include a practical exercise we may ask you to prepare in advance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hiring Manager interview.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bar Raiser interview with leadership stakeholders.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds, experiences, and identities, including those that are traditionally underrepresented in the tech and energy sectors. If you’re excited about this role but not sure you meet every requirement, we’d still love to hear from you. Your unique perspective could be exactly what we’re looking for.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/tem/people-performance-manager-united-kingdom-246305","tags":["People & Talent"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom","created_at":1795156813},{"slug":"operations-manager-operative-acquisition-london-396455","company_name":"Relay","title":"Operations Manager, Operative Acquisition","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Relay is fundamentally reshaping how goods move in an online era.</strong> Backed by Europe’s largest-ever logistics Series A ($35M) led by deep-tech investors Plural, and a recently closed Series B ($95M), Relay is scaling faster than 99% of venture-backed startups. We're assembling the most talent-dense team the logistics industry has ever seen</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Relay’s Mission is</strong> to <strong>free commerce from friction</strong>. Today, high delivery costs act as a hidden tax on e-commerce, quietly shaping what can be sold online and limiting who can participate. We envision a world where <strong>more goods move more freely between more people</strong>, making the online shopping experience seamless and accessible to everyone.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>THE TEAM<br /></strong>• <strong>~160 people</strong>,  around half in engineering, product and data<br />• <strong>45+ advanced degrees</strong> across computer science, mathematics and operations research<br />• <strong>Thousands</strong> of data points captured, calculated, analysed and predicted for every single parcel we handle<br />• An intellectually vibrant culture of <strong>first‑principles thinking</strong>, tight feedback loops and relentless experimentation</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>The role</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every parcel through our sort centres is handled by an operative. At peak, we need to hire up to 600 of them a week.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As <strong>Operations Manager, Operative Acquisition</strong> you'll own operative supply across our sortation sites: enough suitable, trained, compliant and active operatives to fill every shift. You'll build the funnel, reporting and automation that make supply repeatable rather than manual, and keep it ahead of demand as volume rises.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Volumes rise sharply into November and December. Supply, not demand, will be the constraint. This role exists to make sure it isn't.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll be the single owner of the operative funnel, working across acquisition (including paid channels), Live Operations, our site teams, and Product and Engineering, who build the integrations the funnel runs on. You'll write SQL, ship automation, and spend time at our sort centres seeing how new starters actually land.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>What you'll do</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the operative funnel end to end</strong>, from applicant attraction through qualification, training, activation and retention</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Keep applicant supply ahead of site demand</strong>, forecasting how many applicants, training places and sessions are needed and directing spend where gaps exist</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Improve qualification and compliance</strong>, owning Right to Work/KYC and working with Product and Engineering to reduce drop-off and speed up the process</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Optimise training capacity and waitlists</strong>, making sure sessions are filled and candidates stay engaged</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Get new starters onto shift quickly</strong>, supporting activation, shift fill, communications and low-fill processes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reduce cancellations, no-shows and inactivity</strong>, using the root causes to improve communications, processes and policies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own operative communications and compliance processes</strong>, including waitlist messaging, suspensions, strikes and shift-booking comms</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build clear funnel reporting and alerts</strong>, tracking volumes, conversion, time to hire and drop-off by site to identify issues early</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Who Will Thrive in this role?</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A growth or operations background. You treat supply as a daily number and act the same day it slips</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confident in SQL (BigQuery or similar). You build dashboards from raw data, not static trackers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience running a high-volume hiring or onboarding funnel, ideally for a frontline workforce</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A working understanding of Right to Work checks, enough to see how checks and re-checks affect the funnel and operative status. Legal owns the detail, but this can't be a blank</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear writing. You can write processes, requirements and comms that other teams rely on</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience using data to identify trends and improve outcomes”.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Desirable</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with paid acquisition, Google Ads or similar, enough to read performance and brief changes when a site runs short</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience onboarding couriers or drivers at a carrier or delivery platform</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with Product and Engineering on integrations or APIs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with predictive or candidate-quality modelling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong forecasting skills and an understanding of seasonality</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Compensation, Benefits &amp; Workplace</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous equity, richer than 99% of European startups, with annual top-ups to share Relay's success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private health &amp; dental coverage, so comprehensive you'd need to be a partner at a Magic Circle law firm to match it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 days of holidays</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enhanced parental leave</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hardware of your choice</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Extensive perks (gym subsidies, cycle-to-work, Friday office lunch, covered Uber home and dinner for late nights, and more)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Located in Shoreditch, our office set-up enables the kind of in-person interactions that drive impact. We work 4 days on-site, with 1 day remote.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who Thrives at Relay?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Aim with Precision:</strong> You define problems clearly and measure your impact meticulously.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Play to Win:</strong> You chase bold bets, tackle the hard stuff, and view constraints as fuel, not friction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>1% Better Every Day</strong>: You believe that small, consistent improvements lead to exponential growth. You move quickly, deliver results, and learn from every experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>All In, All the Time</strong>: You show up and step up. You take ownership from start to finish and do what it takes to deliver when it counts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>People-Powered Greatness</strong>: You invest in your teammates. You give and receive feedback with care and candour. You build trust through high standards and shared success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow the Whole Pie</strong>: You seek out win-win solutions for merchants, couriers, and our customers, because when they thrive, so do we.<br /><br />If these resonate, and you combine strong technical fundamentals with entrepreneurial drive, let’s connect.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Relay is an <strong>equal-opportunity employer </strong>committed to diversity, inclusion, and fostering a workplace where everyone thrives.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/relay/operations-manager-operative-acquisition-london-396455","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London - On-site","created_at":1795156812},{"slug":"head-of-sales-uk-europe-agentis-asset-management-services-london-340724","company_name":"Agentis Capital Advisors","title":"Head of Sales, UK & Europe — Agentis Asset Management Services","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Firm</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Asset Management Services (“AMS”) is the asset management practice of Agentis Capital Advisors, a global infrastructure advisory and investment platform. AMS manages more than 120 infrastructure assets representing over $35bn in enterprise value across renewables, public-private partnerships, digital and social infrastructure. We support our clients over the life of their assets through four service pillars:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Financial Model Management – We build, standardise, enhance and maintain the financial models behind our clients’ funds and portfolio companies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Financial Services Management – We run the accounting, budgeting, lender compliance and financial reporting for project companies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Operations Management – We oversee the day-to-day management of assets, including contract administration, performance monitoring, and board and stakeholder support</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fund Operations &amp; Reporting – We maintain the fund-level valuation models, NAV and exit calculations, and leadership and LP reporting</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">AMS gives private markets and infrastructure investors one consistent, auditable and trusted view of their portfolios, delivered as a managed service. Our clients include leading infrastructure funds, pension funds, developers and project companies. Our guiding principles of excellence, client success, commitment, people and entrepreneurship set us apart.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Opportunity</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private-markets managers and large asset owners run their portfolios on hundreds of inconsistent models, built by different advisors in different formats. Valuation, investor reporting and portfolio oversight are slow, manual and hard to audit. AMS solves this. We take over a client’s portfolio models, rebuild them to one standard on our technology-enabled platform, and deliver a live, fund-level view of the whole portfolio. We maintain and enhance it with our specialists on an ongoing basis.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a Head of Sales, UK &amp; Europe, based in London, to take this service to market and expand our client base. This is a hands-on, player-coach role, reporting to the Agentis Capital Managing Partners.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role suits a commercially driven seller who has sold value-added services into funds (e.g., fund administration, back-office, data, valuation or portfolio-monitoring software and services), selling to CEOs, heads of asset management, CFOs, COOs and finance teams of private-markets managers. You want to own a territory and build a business, not inherit a book.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our Differentiators</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The first dedicated sales leader for a new AMS service line, shaping how it goes to market from day one</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A differentiated product to sell: an exclusive, technology-enabled modelling and portfolio-reporting platform, delivered by Agentis professionals as a managed service and not as another software licence</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to build on Agentis’s long-standing relationships with infrastructure funds, pension funds and asset owners</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A competitive base plus uncapped commission tied to the recurring revenue you bring in</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The opportunity to hire and lead additional sales professionals as the business grows</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An entrepreneurial culture with a flat structure and direct access to Partners and senior leadership, where good ideas are acted on quickly</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build and Run the UK &amp; European Pipeline</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the UK and European target universe: private-markets fund managers (infrastructure and renewables first, then real estate and private equity), pension and institutional direct investors, and large asset-portfolio owners</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run a disciplined outbound campaign: prioritise and tier targets, secure first meetings and keep a steady weekly cadence of new conversations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use Agentis’s existing relationships, working with Partners to convert warm introductions into qualified opportunities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the CRM accurate as the system of record for contacts, meetings, pipeline stage, forecast and next steps</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Win and Close Mandates</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the full sales cycle, from discovery and demonstrations to pilots, proposals, pricing, negotiation and signed multi-year mandates</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sell to multiple stakeholders: CFOs, COOs, heads of portfolio/asset management, valuation and investor relations, and the risk, IT and procurement teams who must approve the service</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run structured pilots and proofs of concept that turn into paying, recurring engagements</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Address data-security, information-handling and technology questions with the AMS delivery team, including due-diligence questionnaires</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expand existing clients from an initial portfolio into wider fund, valuation and reporting work</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shape the Go-to-Market</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Feed market insight into the sales narrative, buyer personas, objection handling, pricing and packaging</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help develop sales collateral, case studies, demonstrations and the website, using the platform’s outputs as proof points</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent AMS at industry conferences and events across the UK and Europe, and build the service’s profile in the market</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track competitors and adjacent offerings, and report what is winning and losing deals</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build the Sales Team</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">As the business grows, recruit, onboard and lead additional sales professionals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate with the North American sales lead on shared global clients, consistent messaging and pipeline reporting</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner with Delivery</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with the AMS modelling and delivery team so that what is sold can be delivered well and on time</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure a smooth handover from sale to delivery during onboarding, set realistic client expectations and support client change management</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Report weekly to the Partners and AMS steering group on pipeline, conversion, forecast and market feedback</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Skills and Experience</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A substantial and proven track record in B2B sales or business development, including selling value-added services, data or software into funds or institutional investors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selling fund administration, fund accounting, back-office, valuation, portfolio-monitoring, investor-reporting or financial-data solutions to private-markets managers is strongly preferred</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proven ability to open new doors and close complex, consultative, multi-stakeholder sales with long cycles and recurring revenue</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A working understanding of how funds and portfolio companies are valued, modelled and reported</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An existing network of finance and asset management leaders at UK and European private-markets managers, pension funds or asset owners is a strong asset</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort selling a technology-enabled service, and explaining data-security and AI-governance safeguards with credibility to risk-averse buyers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Self-motivated and entrepreneurial: comfortable building process, collateral and pipeline from scratch in a start-up setting within an established firm</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional written and verbal communication and presentation skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Infrastructure, renewables or real-assets experience is an asset</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Compensation and Benefits</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive compensation arrangement including an uncapped commission on recurring revenue</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Eligibility for the Agentis employee ownership programme and access to principal investment opportunities alongside Partners, subject to programme terms</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/agentis-capital-advisors/head-of-sales-uk-europe-agentis-asset-management-services-london-340724","tags":["Asset Management"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1795156812},{"slug":"senior-campaign-manager-temp-contract-london-380823","company_name":"Pleo","title":"Senior Campaign Manager (Temp Contract)","description":"<h2><strong>About Pleo</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Messy spend management is tricky business. And tedious processes are a lose-lose situation for all involved, not just finance. At Pleo, we're changing that. We build spend solutions that make managing money seamless, empowering, and surprisingly effective for finance teams and employees alike - with a vision to help all businesses ‘go beyond’.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The word ‘Pleo’ actually means ‘more than you’d expect’, and living by that mantra has been the secret to our success over the last 10 years.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Now, we’re at a pivotal moment in our journey; every move we make has a direct impact on our 40,000+ customers, our business, and our collective success. We need people who take pride in uncovering customer needs, who turn complex problems into simple solutions, challenge the way things are done (respectfully), and always aim high. With great ambitions driving us forward, we can’t say we’ve got this whole thing figured out. And frankly, that’s half the fun! What we can say is that we’re a driven, progressive, and, importantly, a kind bunch of 850+ people from over 100 nationalities, all committed to delivering the future of business spending, together.</p><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a Senior Integrated Campaign Manager, Brand &amp; GTM to join our Integrated Marketing team at Pleo. In this role, you'll help architect, roll out, project manage, and drive the Go-To-Market (GTM) execution for our major 2027 brand marketing strategy and campaigns and be part of turning brand strategy, positioning, and creative concepts into operational GTM blueprints as we scale our multi-segment (SMB, Mid-Market, Enterprise) reach across 6 key European markets. If you're excited about high-visibility, full-funnel orchestration and balancing long-term brand equity building with full-funnel conversion, and are passionate about integrated brand and GTM marketing in high-growth B2B SaaS, then this is the opportunity for you!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Please bear in mind this role is a temporary contract of 1 year. </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who you’ll be working with and reporting to </strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll report to our Director of Integrated Marketing and work closely with teams in Brand Marketing, Digital, Field/Events, Content, PR, Product Marketing (PMM), Marketing Ops, Data, and Sales/Growth channels. Our team is highly collaborative and dedicated to bridging top-of-funnel brand awareness with lower-funnel acquisition, ensuring every campaign moment translates into market salience, customer engagement, and measurable business impact. You’ll also have the chance to partner with teams across country teams, local market stakeholders, Sales Leadership, SDRs, and Field squads to ensure success.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll be doing</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Senior Campaign Manager, you will: </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Integrated GTM Architecture &amp; Strategic Planning</strong>: Translate the overarching 2027 brand strategy into actionable, full-funnel GTM campaign blueprints across SMB, Mid-Market, and Enterprise segments, architecting campaign flighting and distribution models across 6 European markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The "Master Brief" &amp; Cross-Functional Squad Leadership</strong>: Own and author comprehensive Integrated Campaign Master Briefs, leading the operational rhythm of cross-functional squads to execute multi-channel strategies (OOH, Paid Social, VIP activations, Digital, ABM) on time and within scope.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Localization &amp; Regional Adaptation</strong>: Partner with country teams and local market stakeholders to ensure master campaign frameworks balance global consistency with local relevance and execution precision.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strategic Brand Partnership &amp; Enablement</strong>: Serve as the strategic execution peer to the Brand Marketing Lead, while partnering with Sales Leadership, SDRs, and Field teams to equip customer-facing squads with the stories, tools, and campaign momentum needed to capitalize on campaign-generated intent.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Campaign Operations, Budget &amp; ROI Accountability</strong>: Maintain and protect the integrated campaign master calendar, manage and allocate the multi-country integrated campaign budget, and partner with Marketing Ops, Data, and Brand Intelligence to track brand lift, consideration, pipeline growth, and closed-won impact.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you bring</strong> </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />You’ll thrive in this role if you have:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proven track record leading multi-million dollar, multi-country, full-funnel integrated campaigns in high-growth B2B SaaS or tech environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep experience taking high-level brand frameworks and translating them into multi-channel GTM blueprints across varied audience segments (SMB to Enterprise).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High proficiency in aligning cross-functional teams (Creative, Digital, PR, Ops, Sales) and holding squads accountable to tight deadlines and complex campaign launches.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep understanding of how to run campaigns across diverse European markets, with a clear perspective on modular campaign design and local adaptation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with tracking brand-to-pipeline performance metrics, campaign flighting dynamics, brand lift, consideration, and total ROI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A background in integrated marketing, GTM campaign management, or brand marketing orchestration within B2B technology or SaaS.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why is this role a good fit for you</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is a good fit for you if:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You thrive as the operational bridge between high-level brand strategy and lower-funnel demand generation, turning concepts into structured GTM blueprints.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You love leading cross-functional squads across multiple international markets, balancing consistency with local nuances across 6 key European countries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You take pride in end-to-end accountability, from authoring master briefs and handling multi-country budgets to tracking downstream pipeline velocity and closed-won revenue impact.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is not a good fit for you if:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You prefer focusing purely on high-level creative ideation, copy, or audience insight development without building the operational execution machinery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You prefer running single-channel or single-market marketing initiatives rather than orchestrating complex, multi-segment (SMB to Enterprise), multi-channel matrices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are uncomfortable navigating data, campaign flighting performance, budget allocations, and downstream pipeline attribution alongside brand metrics.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>How you’ll develop in this role </strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">In your first 6 months at Pleo, you’ll:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the architecture and rollout of the 2027 integrated brand campaign calendar across all target European markets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with the Brand Marketing Lead, country teams, and Marketing Ops to stand up the Master Briefing framework and streamline cross-functional execution rhythms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Grow your skills in full-funnel orchestration and multi-market scale, driving measurable brand lift, consideration, and downstream pipeline velocity as Pleo continues to expand.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The location</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Please note: We can hire on a hybrid or in-person set-up in any of the locations listed on the advert but <u>you will need to be physically based in the country of your choice with a valid right to work</u>. We are <u>unable to offer visa sponsorship for this role</u> in any of the listed locations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Show me the benefits!</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your own Pleo card (no more out-of-pocket spending!)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lunch is on us for your work days - enjoy catered meals or receive a lunch allowance based on your local office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive private healthcare - depending on your location, coverage options include Vitality, Alan or Médis</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 days of annual leave + public holidays (additional days may apply in select countries based on local standards).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">For our Team, we offer both hybrid and fully remote working options</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We use MyndUp to give our employees access to free mental health and well-being support with great success so far</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paid parental leave - we want to make sure that we're supportive of families and help you feel that you don't have to compromise your family due to work</p></li></ul><h2><strong><br />The interview process</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We want to ensure you are set-up for success and understand what will be expected of you. If your application is successful, our interview process is as follows:</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Intro call: </strong>A 30-minute chat with our Talent Partner to discuss the role and your background.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hiring Manager Interview:</strong> A 45 minute chat to deep dive into your experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Challenge &amp; Team Interview:</strong> We will send you a take home test and invite you to present during a 60 minute team interview. This is an opportunity to show us how you would handle the day to day of the role</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Final Interview</strong>: A final interview with a senior leader</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em">Transparency is important to us so we also wanted to share some insights about what we’re looking for in applications to ensure you can set yourself up for success!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Last time we hired for this role, we received a total vast number of applications but only a few were selected for an intro call.Some of the key reasons why previous candidates didn’t make it past the application screening stage include:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CV writing and content: we receive a lot of CVs, and many of them are AI-generated. We love seeing people leverage AI—it’s a big focus for us internally too—but without human intervention, these CVs can sometimes become generic and fail to show a candidate in the best light. What we're really looking for is the specific details of real impact that only you know from your previous experience. A top tip from us is to use the “Achieved X, as measured by Y, by doing Z” formula (credit: Laszlo Bock, ~2014) to give a really clear picture of what you’ve worked on. A final note: including links to your previous companies' websites is a huge help and allows us to truly understand your background!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Application care: every single application we receive is reviewed by a human (yes, hundreds of them) because we believe that candidates' efforts should be matched by an equal level of human care. This means that we expect a similar level of attention put into your application. Read and answer the application questions carefully, they make a huge difference in our decision-making process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Profile to role fit: highlight most important aspects of the role, points that might get misunderstood, any specific industry requirements etc.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>About your application</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>English first.</strong> Since it's our company language, please submit your application in English. You’ll be using it a lot if you join us.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A fair look for everyone.</strong> Our talent team reads every single application to ensure the process is fair. To keep things running smoothly, we only accept applications through our system—our support team can’t pass on calls or emails.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Diversity drives us.</strong> We can only reach our goals if our team reflects the world around us. That starts with you hitting apply, even if you don't tick every single box. We encourage people from all backgrounds and experiences to join us.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Interview at your best.</strong> We want you to feel comfortable throughout the process. If you have any accessibility requirements or need a specific format, email ----- We’ll design a process that works for you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your data is safe.</strong> When you apply, we process your personal data as a data processor. For more information on how Pleo processes personal data, read our Privacy Policy <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="in-cell-link" href="https://www.pleo.io/en/legal"><u>here</u></a>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Applying for multiple roles?</strong> Nothing is stopping you, and we assess every role independently. However, we do look for alignment, so make sure you can explain why your interest and experience are right for each specific role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reapplying.</strong> If you’re applying for the same role again, please wait six months from your last decision before hitting submit.</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/pleo/senior-campaign-manager-temp-contract-london-380823","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1795156812},{"slug":"workplace-technology-specialist-london-181016","company_name":"Legora","title":"Workplace Technology Specialist - London","description":"<h2>About Us</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Legora is redefining how legal work gets done. Not built for lawyers, built with them. We work alongside the world’s best legal teams, who expect excellence, precision, and speed, and we hold ourselves to the same bar.<br /><br />Our AI-native workspace lets legal professionals move faster, think more clearly, and operate with sharper precision. By analysing thousands of documents in minutes and powering end-to-end workflows, we cut through complexity, teams can focus on what matters: judgment, strategy, and outcomes.<br /><br />2,100+ customers across 80+ countries trust us, including Cleary Gottlieb, Goodwin, Linklaters, White &amp; Case, Dentons, and Barclays. We’ve scaled to<strong> $200M+ in ARR</strong>, with teams across Europe, North America and APAC, and continue to expand through acquisitions including Qura, Walter AI, Graceview, Cadastral, and Wexler.<br /><br />We partner with world-class performers: including Aaron Judge and the New York Yankees, Ludvig Åberg (and his caddie), and campaigns featuring Jude Law.<br /><br />Joining Legora means three things.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We <strong>lean in: </strong>ownership over titles, outcomes over intentions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We <strong>fight for excellence:</strong> high standards, direct, ego-free feedback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We<strong> grow together:</strong> as a team and with our customers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mission before ego. Everyone contributes. No one coasts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re driven by impact, pace, and raising the bar. This is the place.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">London | Full-time | Onsite, five days a week</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reports to the Workplace Technology Lead</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>THE ROLE</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The IT and AI Enablement function exists to make Legora itself run as well as the product we sell: secure, automated, and improving over time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our Workplace Technology Specialist in London, you'll help keep the technology our employees use every day working smoothly, from laptops and onboarding to meeting rooms and office connectivity. You'll report to our Workplace Technology Lead and work closely with Workplace, Office Managers, EAs, and the wider IT team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on individual contributor role. You'll take ownership of everyday support requests, follow issues through to resolution, and help deliver office technology projects with direction from the Workplace Technology Lead. It's an opportunity to build your technical skills while making a visible difference to how our London office runs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>WHAT YOU'LL BE DOING</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be a helpful, responsive first point of contact for employees. Troubleshoot laptop, application, account, peripheral, and connectivity issues through our shared service desk and in person. Keep people informed and escalate complex issues with clear diagnostics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help new hires get productive from day one: stage devices, complete approved account and access setup, check equipment, and introduce colleagues to Legora's tools. Support offboarding and equipment returns using established processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep meeting rooms ready to use. Run regular AV checks, troubleshoot conferencing equipment, and support all-hands, events, and important meetings alongside the Workplace Technology Lead and the relevant teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the local hardware lifecycle, including provisioning, inventory, loaners, repairs, replacements, and returns. Keep asset records accurate and flag stock needs early.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Troubleshoot basic office Wi-Fi and wired connectivity problems. Gather useful information and work with the Workplace Technology Lead and the IT Systems team on issues that need deeper investigation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assist with office moves, desk setups, equipment installations, and vendor visits. Follow agreed checklists, test the work, and raise issues for the Workplace Technology Lead to resolve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help maintain badge readers, cameras, and other office technology by identifying faults and coordinating fixes under established processes. Security owns access policy and monitoring.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write clear support guides and improve repeatable tasks. Help test practical automation and AI-assisted support workflows with the team so common issues become easier to prevent and resolve.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>WHO 