tyle="min-height:1.5em">If that excites you, how about joining our ClearBank Europe’s Operations team as a Senior Credit &amp; Risk Associate?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reporting directly to the Director of Operations, you will be at the centre of the day-to-day credit lifecycle. You will own and execute the core credit assessment, monitoring and provisioning activities that support sound lending decisions, and you will coordinate the information and hand-offs required across Sales, Finance &amp; Treasury, and Risk. Alongside this, you will support the management of ClearBank Europe’s operational risk environment, risks and controls, operational risk events, issues and actions, and evidence of control effectiveness across the Operations function. The role in a nutshell: you produce, operate and coordinate the first-line credit process; working closely with second line as they provide independent review and challenge.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your role includes:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Creditworthiness assessment and underwriting</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the creditworthiness assessment model specifications and the supporting assessment tool, keeping the methodology and practical execution aligned.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Execute creditworthiness assessments for onboarding and periodic reviews, including gathering and assessing the required client inputs and translating the outcome into a clear credit conclusion.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare the first-line overdraft / credit proposal, inc luding the proposed limit and the analysis supporting the recommendation, and coordinate the proposal through the relevant approval process.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate credit onboarding once approved, ensuring agreed credit terms and the relevant operational hand-offs are clear to the teams involved.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Early warning, portfolio monitoring &amp; provisioning</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own and operate the Early Warning Indicator assessment process and investigate triggered cases.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain visibility of Watch List and Default cases, ensuring appropriate escalation and hand-off.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Produce first-line credit risk monitoring across the portfolio, identifying changes in exposure, concentrations and emerging risks.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate annual credit reviews, renewals and exits.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support NPE and forbearance management through appropriate first-line analysis, case history and supporting data.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Credit risk framework and pricing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain the first-line Credit Risk / Credit Underwriting framework and supporting operating procedures.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate relevant policy requirements into practical processes, tools, controls and monitoring.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate periodic review of relevant interest-rate spreads and overdraft fees with Finance &amp; Treasury.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify opportunities to improve the efficiency, consistency and control of the credit process.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Risk &amp; Controls</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the ongoing development of Operations risk and control within ClearBank Europe, ensuring operational risks, controls and residual-risk assessments remain current, appropriately evidenced and aligned to risk appetite.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with risk and control owners to assess inherent risk, control design and effectiveness, and residual risk, providing constructive first-line challenge where required.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain oversight of locally operated, Group and outsourced controls, ensuring ClearBank Europe has appropriate evidence and entity-level oversight.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support the management of operational incidents, control weaknesses, issues and remediation actions, ensuring root causes and lessons learned feed back into the RCSA and control environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What does success in this role look like?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Credit assessments and proposals are timely, well evidenced and decision-ready, with a clear audit trail from client information through to conclusion and limit recommendation.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Daily EWI monitoring and annual reviews operate reliably, with Watch List, Default, renewal and exit cases identified and progressed without unnecessary delay.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The first-line credit framework, models and tools remain practical, current and consistently applied as the lending portfolio develops.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stakeholders have a clear view of case status, responsibilities and next steps because you actively coordinate the credit lifecycle rather than simply completing individual analyses.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">There is clear separation between first-line ownership and second-line independent challenge, while the two roles work together effectively to keep the portfolio within approved risk appetite.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Robust, current and well-evidenced operational risk and control environment, proactively identifying emerging risks and control weaknesses and ensuring appropriate actions are taken to address them.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll bring: </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience in credit analysis, underwriting, portfolio monitoring or a closely related first-line credit role within banking or regulated financial services.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong ability to analyse financial and non-financial information and convert it into a concise, evidence-based credit view and recommendation.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of business or institutional lending products and the risk drivers associated with limits, overdrafts or comparable credit exposures.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical understanding of early-warning monitoring, Watch List / Default concepts and the credit lifecycle from onboarding through periodic review, renewal and exit.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of IFRS 9 provisioning and staging, with the ability to operate models and investigate or explain outcomes. Model ownership or methodology experience is an advantage.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Having some financial crime risk background within a regulated institution is also nice to have.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong organisation and stakeholder coordination skills. You are comfortable driving inputs and actions across Sales, Operations, Finance &amp; Treasury, Risk and governance forums.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A can-do attitude geared to execution, with strong attention to detail and the judgement to know when an issue needs escalation.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort working in a growing bank where processes and products continue to evolve, and the willingness to improve them as you go.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What makes a great ClearBank team member?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You focus on solutions and positive outcomes, thinking radically and responsibly about the best result for customers, colleagues and the bank.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You seek feedback, assume positive intent and build strong, trusting relationships.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You care about quality, but you also know that progress matters: you learn, iterate and improve.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">'I' before 'we' is not in your vocabulary. You succeed through clear ownership and collaboration</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer in return:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're flexible – We support a culture of flexibility which allows our employees to achieve a strong work-life balance.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offices – Work in a way that works for you, combining working from our Amsterdam office with working from home.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Holiday – 27 days of annual leave per year, plus public holidays.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Holiday buy/sell - Buy or sell up to five days of annual leave each year and shape your year around what matters most.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work abroad – You have the flexibility to work outside of the Netherlands for up to 30 days in a rolling 12-month period.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Socials – Regular social events open to all.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Holiday swap – Option to swap your bank holidays to any other day of your choice.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wellbeing – long term disability cover and accident cover.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bigger than ClearBank – Take a couple of days per year to do something that matters to you.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension – We offer generous pension contribution without mandatory employee contribution.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expense coverage – Mobile phone allowance and travel cost reimbursement.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Family – Enhanced family-friendly leave.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Personal development – We offer personal development budgets, opportunities to take part in role-related training and unlimited