uiters learning more about the role and ClearBank, and we’ll get it know more about you, your experience and how your skills align with the role (this will be via phone or Teams video call). You can expect to hear back from us within seven days following this meeting (if things are taking longer than expected, we’ll let you know that too); </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First Interview:</strong> You’ll spend one hour with a member of our hiring team focusing on your skills, competencies and your ways of working at the same time we’ll give you time to ask more questions about the role, the team and learn more about the ClearBank culture. This will be via Teams.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Second Interview:</strong> This will be a competency-based interview with one or more members of our team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Final Stage: </strong>You will have a final meeting with the Head of Department. This will be around 45-60 minutes.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Offer:</strong> Congratulations! Get ready to transform banking forever! </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our commitment to you as a candidate:</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We will always try our best to get back to you within seven days of your interview whether you’ve been successful or not and provide you with feedback. Sometimes things take a little longer, so we may not have a decision to share but we will get it touch to let you know we need a little more time.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re unable to provide specific individual feedback at the application or screening stage but know that your application was reviewed and considered carefully.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We wish you the best of luck with your application and maybe we’ll be celebrating your new role at ClearBank soon!  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equal Opportunities</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">ClearBank is committed to ensuring equal opportunities throughout every stage of the recruitment process. ClearBank recognises that diversity is vital to the long-term success of the business in the communities and markets in which it operates. ClearBank is also a firm believer that an inclusive culture fosters greater employee engagement and collaboration. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">ClearBank strives for diversity and inclusion of all forms, including (but not limited to): gender, age, educational and professional background, disability, gender reassignment, marital or civil partner status, pregnancy or maternity, race, colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin, religion or belief and sexual orientation. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As part of the Company’s commitment to equal employment opportunity, we provide reasonable adjustments, to candidates during the recruitment process, including to individuals with disabilities. We want to create a safe space that welcomes everyone so please let us know how we can accommodate you. In case you have any accessibility requirements you can share that with our Talent Acquisition team prior to your interview stage, if applicable. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The legal bit</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">By submitting your CV to ClearBank Limited you are providing your consent for us to use the information you provide for recruitment purposes. For more information on how we manage your data go and check out our Candidate Privacy Notice on the ClearBank website to see how we process, manage and look after your data. You are also allowing us to communicate with you by email and telephone for recruitment purposes. </p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/clearbank/senior-credit-risk-associate-amsterdam-353616","tags":["ClearBank Europe"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam Office - Hybrid","created_at":1795167613},{"slug":"credit-and-financial-risk-manager-amsterdam-52165","company_name":"Clearbank","title":"Credit and Financial Risk Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">We built ClearBank on the belief that banking infrastructure would no longer slow down progress. Instead, it would be a catalyst that unlocks the potential to innovate. It would adapt to different needs so a new era in financial services could begin. We’re here to challenge the status quo in banking, are you?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We all know that transforming banking forever is not an easy mission, but we’re more than ready to rise to that challenge. We all do it every day; navigating new, unexpected and sometimes even daunting challenges. But we believe in ourselves and trust we can do it. Want to innovate? Go for it. Push for a better way? You Can. If you think you have it in you, this is Where You Can. ClearBank is a place where you can do things differently and challenge the status quo. We will give you a high level of autonomy and transparency, and we trust you to make the right decisions for the bank.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you can expect:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">ClearBank is a place where you can do things differently and challenge the status quo. We will give you a high level of autonomy and transparency, and we trust you to make the right decisions for the bank.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If that excites you, how about joining our Risk team as a Credit and Financial Risk Manager?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reporting to the Chief Risk Officer, you will lead independent second-line oversight of ClearBank's lending and financial risk activities. As a senior risk leader and recognised subject-matter expert, you will translate Risk strategy into business-critical delivery, shape appetite, policy, controls and governance, and influence material decisions across ClearBank Europe and the wider Group. You will provide authoritative challenge, anticipate emerging issues, lead complex remediation and recovery activity, and strengthen organisational capability while enabling sustainable growth.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your role includes: </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide independent second-line oversight and challenge across the design, approval, launch and ongoing management of lending products, ensuring material risks are understood, controlled and aligned with approved appetite.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the second-line review and challenge of complex or material credit proposals, portfolio strategies and periodic reviews, providing clear recommendations to senior decision-makers and governance committees.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the second-line approach to non-performing and vulnerable exposures, leading complex recovery strategies, senior stakeholder engagement, escalation and resolution to minimise losses and protect ClearBank's interests.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape and maintain the policy, appetite, control and governance framework across the credit lifecycle, partnering with model validation and other specialists to ensure credit risk and provisioning models remain robust and fit for purpose.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide senior oversight of financial risks, including asset and liability, liquidity and interest-rate risk, connecting risk assessments across disciplines and anticipating emerging balance-sheet vulnerabilities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead complex, cross-functional risk initiatives with potential enterprise application, translating strategy and regulatory expectations into practical improvements across ClearBank Europe and the wider ClearBank Group.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What does success in this role look like:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain a high-quality lending portfolio that enables sustainable growth within risk appetite.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver forward-looking credit and financial risk insight that improves senior and committee decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Resolve complex and emerging risks issues, including non-performing exposures, through decisive intervention, recovery and escalation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape scalable policies, appetite, controls and governance for growth and regulatory change.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a recognised expert and trusted adviser, influencing senior stakeholders through expertise, sound judgement and constructive challenge.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Align functions on competing priorities, ownership and enterprise risk outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build capability through coaching, delegation and knowledge sharing.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To excel in this role, you’ll also need:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Extensive experience leading second-line challenge of complex credit risk in regulated financial services.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of launching and scaling credit products within robust risk governance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advanced expertise in institutional lending, portfolios, problem exposures and risk drivers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong knowledge of liquidity, interest-rate and asset-and-liability risk.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to lead complex work independently and improve risk outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional analytical and communication skills, with credibility among senior stakeholders and committees.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leadership experience in coaching, setting standards and creating accountability.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What makes a great ClearBank team member? Does this sound like you?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You focus on solutions and positive outcomes, thinking radically and responsibly to find the best result for our customers, your colleagues and the bank.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You actively seek feedback from others to drive your growth and development, always assuming positive intent from others and develop strong, trusting relationships you’re your colleagues and customers: you really, genuinely care.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You always strive for the highest quality, but you know that done is better than perfect; you welcome a challenge knowing that they learn as you go and iterate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">‘I’ before ’we’, isn’t in your vocabulary.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">If this sounds like you then we encourage you to dust off that CV and apply!</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer in return: </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're flexible – We support a culture of flexibility which allows our employees to achieve a strong work-life balance. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offices – Work in a way that works for you, combining working from our Amsterdam office with working from home.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Holiday – 27 days of annual leave per year, plus public holidays.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Holiday buy/sell - Buy or sell up to five days of annual leave each year and shape your year around what matters most.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work abroad – You have the flexibility to work outside of the Netherlands for up to 30 days in a rolling 12-month period.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Socials – Regular social events open to all.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Holiday swap – Option to swap your bank holidays to any other day of your choice.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wellbeing – long term disability cover and accident cover.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bigger than ClearBank – Take a couple of days per year to do something that matters to you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension – We offer generous pension contribution without mandatory employee contribution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expense coverage – Mobile phone allowance and travel cost reimbursement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Family – Enhanced family-friendly leave.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Personal development – We offer personal development budgets, opportunities to take part in role-related training and unlimited LinkedIn Learning.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">And not forgetting the biggest benefit of all. The opportunity to be part of an incredible team that’s building a tech-bank fit for the future.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Role level: 5</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A little bit more about us!</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ClearBank is Where You Can belong:</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At ClearBank we think about Diversity, Equity and Inclusion (DE&amp;I) a lot. Not because we think we should. But because we know we should – how else can we build a happy workforce and be successful as a business. We’re committed to making sure our teams reflect society. And we put energy and effort into making this a place where everyone feels at home, where they’re given the trust and encouragement to do their very best work. Here are some of the things we’re most proud of: </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">42% of our senior management roles are held by women </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our enhanced family leave policies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Launching our partnership with Code First Girls </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Increasing awareness of neurodiversity in the workplace through our partnership with the Inclusive Group </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our hiring process and what you can expect:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Application:</strong> a member of our talent acquisition team will review your application against the key requirements for the role and let you know within two weeks whether you’re moving forward to the next stage; </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Screening:</strong> You’ll spend 30-45 minutes speaking to one of our recruiters learning more about the role and ClearBank, and we’ll get it know more about you, your experience and how your skills align with the role (this will be via phone or Teams video call). You can expect to hear back from us within seven days following this meeting (if things are taking longer than expected, we’ll let you know that too); </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First Interview:</strong> You’ll spend one hour with a member of our hiring team focusing on your skills, competencies and your ways of working at the same time we’ll give you time to ask more questions about the role, the team and learn more about the ClearBank culture. This will be via Teams.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Second Interview:</strong> This will be a competency-based interview with one or more members of our team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Final Stage: </strong>You will have a final meeting with the Head of Department. This will be around 45-60 minutes.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Offer:</strong> Congratulations! Get ready to transform banking forever! </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our commitment to you as a candidate:</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We will always try our best to get back to you within seven days of your interview whether you’ve been successful or not and provide you with feedback. Sometimes things take a little longer, so we may not have a decision to share but we will get it touch to let you know we need a little more time.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re unable to provide specific individual feedback at the application or screening stage but know that your application was reviewed and considered carefully.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We wish you the best of luck with your application and maybe we’ll be celebrating your new role at ClearBank soon!  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equal Opportunities</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">ClearBank is committed to ensuring equal opportunities throughout every stage of the recruitment process. ClearBank recognises that diversity is vital to the long-term success of the business in the communities and markets in which it operates. ClearBank is also a firm believer that an inclusive culture fosters greater employee engagement and collaboration. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">ClearBank strives for diversity and inclusion of all forms, including (but not limited to): gender, age, educational and professional background, disability, gender reassignment, marital or civil partner status, pregnancy or maternity, race, colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin, religion or belief and sexual orientation. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As part of the Company’s commitment to equal employment opportunity, we provide reasonable adjustments, to candidates during the recruitment process, including to individuals with disabilities. We want to create a safe space that welcomes everyone so please let us know how we can accommodate you. In case you have any accessibility requirements you can share that with our Talent Acquisition team prior to your interview stage, if applicable. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The legal bit</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">By submitting your CV to ClearBank Limited you are providing your consent for us to use the information you provide for recruitment purposes. For more information on how we manage your data go and check out our Candidate Privacy Notice on the ClearBank website to see how we process, manage and look after your data. You are also allowing us to communicate with you by email and telephone for recruitment purposes. </p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/clearbank/credit-and-financial-risk-manager-amsterdam-52165","tags":["ClearBank Europe"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam Office - Hybrid","created_at":1795167613},{"slug":"remote-senior-account-manager-warehouse-automation-benelux-netherlands-21998","company_name":"Exotec","title":"Senior Account Manager - Warehouse Automation - BENELUX","description":"<p>At Exotec, we design elegant, plug-and-play, and reliable end-to-end warehouse robotics solutions. As a leading Original Equipment Manufacturer (OEM) and Integrator, we support some of the world’s most iconic brands in their transition to automation. We’re proud to design technology that doesn’t just redefine intralogistics; it also makes warehouses safer, faster, more efficient, and less physically demanding for the people working inside them.</p><p></p><h2>Why this role matters</h2><p>Ready to move the world of intralogistics with tech? Join us as a Service Account Manager. </p><p></p><h3>What You'll Do </h3><p>We are looking for individuals who put customers first, take ownership of their work, execute with rigor, and simplify complex challenges. Successful team members demonstrate a continuous improvement mindset, collaborate effectively across functions, and contribute to collective success. At Exotec, we value people who are proactive, transparent, respectful, adaptable, and committed to delivering excellence while building long-term trust with both customers and colleagues.</p><p></p><ul><li>Own the strategic relationship with a portfolio of customers, serving as their primary point of contact for service performance, escalations, and long-term success.</li><li>Lead regular business reviews and governance meetings with customers, ensuring transparency on KPIs, system performance, ongoing actions, and improvement plans.</li><li>Partner closely with Area Managers, Maintenance teams, Product, Performance Engineering, and Support functions to resolve customer concerns and drive operational excellence.</li><li>Act as the voice of the customer internally, translating customer feedback and business needs into actionable improvement initiatives.</li><li>Identify risks, challenges, and opportunities within customer accounts, coordinating proactive action plans to maintain customer satisfaction and contract performance.</li><li>Support customer growth by identifying upselling opportunities, service extensions, and additional value-added solutions aligned with customer needs.</li><li>Oversee the successful transition of customer sites from Deployment to Maintenance, ensuring a seamless handover and clear ownership model.</li><li>Monitor contractual performance, service levels, and commercial commitments while ensuring alignment between customer expectations and operational delivery.</li><li>Drive continuous improvement initiatives that enhance system reliability, service quality, and the overall customer experience.</li><li>Build trusted relationships with key customer stakeholders, from operational teams to senior leadership, acting as a long-term partner to their business.</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Experience in Account Management, Customer Success, Operations Management, Supply Chain, Logistics, Warehouse Operations, or Service Delivery.</li><li>Strong customer-facing skills and experience managing demanding stakeholders.</li><li>Ability to navigate complex organizations and coordinate cross-functional teams.</li><li>Commercial awareness with the ability to identify growth opportunities within existing accounts.</li><li>Experience working in logistics, warehouse automation, intralogistics, manufacturing, industrial services, or a similar environment is highly valued.</li><li>Excellent communication, influencing, and problem-solving skills.</li><li>Fluent English required; additional languages are a plus.</li></ul><p></p><h2>Why you’ll love working here </h2><ul><li>Make an impact by building technology that improves business performance and people's everyday work.&nbsp;</li></ul><ul><li>Grow faster by solving complex challenges in a fast-moving company where innovation, speed and ambition accelerate your development.&nbsp;</li></ul><ul><li>Belong to a global team where diversity, inclusion and collaboration drive better decisions and stronger solutions.&nbsp;</li></ul><ul><li>Connect beyond work by sharing passions, celebrating milestones and building lasting relationships that strengthen the way we work together.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/exotec/remote-senior-account-manager-warehouse-automation-benelux-netherlands-2199