&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-CA&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot;&gt;Please read our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.wppmedia.com/pages/privacy-policy#:~:text=WPP%20Media%20Privacy%20Notice%20for%20Recruitment&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-CA&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot;&gt;for more information on how we process the information you provide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP SCXW227196529 BCX8&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:276}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/wppmedia/global-client-director-amsterdam-289582","tags":["Client Teams"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795136126},{"slug":"stage-consumentengedrag-amsterdam-309917","company_name":"Growy Group BV","title":"Stage Consumentengedrag","description":"<p>Waarom pak je in de supermarkt het ene product wel uit het schap en het andere niet? Ligt het aan de verpakking? De prijs? Smaak? Gemak? Of simpelweg omdat het precies op de juiste plek staat?</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Bij Growy telen we verse sla, kruiden en microgreens in Amsterdam in onze vertical farm. Vertical farming klinkt misschien ingewikkeld, maar het idee is simpel: we telen planten in lagen boven elkaar, midden in de stad en helemaal los van het weer buiten.<br>Nu onze producten in steeds meer Nederlandse supermarkten te vinden zijn, willen we onze consumenten nóg beter leren begrijpen. Daarom zoeken we een nieuwsgierige en commercieel ingestelde stagiair die zich wil verdiepen in consumentengedrag en inzichten kan vertalen naar echte commerciële kansen.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>En nee, dit wordt geen stageproject wat ergens in een lade verdwijnt en niemand ooit nog bekijkt, jouw stage gaat voor ons echt een verschil maken! <br><br>🌱<strong>Wat ga je doen?</strong> </p><p>Hoe zorgen we ervoor dat meer consumenten Growy ontdekken, proberen én opnieuw kopen?</p><p>Tijdens je stage ga je bijvoorbeeld:</p><ul><li><p>consumenten interviewen en/of focusgroepen organiseren;</p></li><li><p>onderzoeken wat mensen belangrijk vinden bij het kopen van verse salades en kruiden;</p></li><li><p>ontdekken welke drempels consumenten ervan weerhouden een product te proberen;</p></li><li><p>onderzoeken wat juist zorgt voor een herhaalaankoop;</p></li><li><p>kijken naar kansen rondom prijs, assortiment, verpakking, positionering, promoties en zichtbaarheid;</p></li><li><p>kwantitatief onderzoek, zoals enquêtes, opzetten om ideeën te testen;</p></li><li><p>jouw inzichten vertalen naar concrete commerciële en marketingaanbevelingen.</p></li></ul><p>Aan het einde van je stage presenteer je jouw belangrijkste inzichten en aanbevelingen aan ons Sales &amp; Marketing team. En als het binnen je stage past, kun je misschien zelfs één van je ideeën in de praktijk testen.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>De precieze inhoud stemmen we af op de duur van je stage en de eisen vanuit jouw opleiding.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Goed om te weten; onze farm is nog volop in ontwikkeling, we zitten nog in onze start-up/scale-up fase. Dit betekent dat je naast je onderzoek ook tijd zult besteden aan andere zaken in onze farm. Dit geldt niet alleen voor jou als stagiair maar voor ons hele team. Zo draait iedereen uit kantoor maandelijks een shift in de farm, waarbij we helpen met zaaien, oogsten of verpakken.<br><br>🌱<strong>Wat kun je van ons verwachten?</strong></p><ul><li><p>Een unieke stageplek; wij bouwen aan de toekomst van voedselproductie;</p></li><li><p>Je wordt onderdeel van een klein team, er wordt naar je ideëen en input geluisterd; </p></li><li><p>We werken fulltime vanaf onze farm in Amsterdam;</p></li><li><p>Een maandelijkse stagevergoeding van 500 euro, we vergoeden geen andere zaken;</p></li><li><p>Veel ruimte en tijd voor creativiteit en een ‘ga het maar proberen!' mentaliteit</p></li><li><p>Een gezellige werksfeer waarin we graag samen na werk nog leuke dingen ondernemen</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>🌱<strong>Wat breng jij? </strong></p><ul><li><p>Je volgt een HBO of WO opleiding in Nederland en staat daar ingeschreven gedurende de hele stage periode. Qua studies denken wij in de richting marketing, bedrijfskunde of (commerciële) psychologie, maar wie weet volg jij een andere studie die ook goed aansluit 🙂</p></li><li><p>Fulltime beschikbaar voor 4 of 5 maanden, startdatum december 2026 of januari of februari 2027</p></li><li><p>Je hebt je rijbewijs B; je zult veel op pad zijn om supermarkten te bezoeken</p></li><li><p>Een flinke portie nieuwsgierigheid </p></li><li><p>Je bent sociaal; je stapt makkelijk op mensen af en maakt een praatje met ze</p></li><li><p>Je spreekt vloeiend Nederlands en kunt je ook goed redden in het Engels</p></li><li><p>Je bent een zelf-starter; we zullen je uiteraard begeleiden tijdens je stage, maar het initiatief voor de invulling en aanpak ligt bij jou</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/growy-group-bv/stage-consumentengedrag-amsterdam-309917","tags":["Marketing & Sales"],"job_types":["Student college","internship"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1795135898},{"slug":"product-manager-insurance-pc-amsterdam-124103","company_name":"Insify","title":"Product Manager Insurance P&C","description":"<p>Insify is looking for a smart, ambitious and relentlessly driven <strong>Insurance Product Manager</strong> to join our team. In this role you’ll be a driving force behind our product expansions and building the digital platform for SME insurance. A rare opportunity to take real ownership in a fast-scaling European insurtech and shape outcomes that matter.</p>
<p>At Insify, we build insurance for entrepreneurs because we are entrepreneurs ourselves. We know what it’s like to build something from scratch, to take risks, and to carry responsibility that doesn’t switch off at 5 pm.</p>
<p>Our mission is simple but ambitious: <strong>to make business insurance 10x simpler, faster, and fairer for entrepreneurs and SMEs across Europe</strong>. No paperwork. No fine print. No legacy complexity. Just modern software, smart automation, and a relentless focus on the customer.</p>
<p>We are a <strong>high-growth European scale-up</strong>, backed by <strong>€43M from world-class investors</strong>, on a mission to become a global leader in digital insurance for entrepreneurs and SMEs. Starting in the Netherlands, we’ve expanded into France and Germany, and we’re only accelerating from here.</p>
<p>At our core, we’re a <strong>tech company</strong>. We build our own insurtech platform and rely heavily on data, automation, and AI to redesign the end-to-end insurance experience:&nbsp; from underwriting to claims. Combined with a fully digital customer portal and strong UX, we’re turning insurance into something surprisingly simple, transparent, and fair.</p>
<p>We’re led by seasoned entrepreneurs who’ve built and scaled companies before, and we bring that same ambition, urgency, and ownership mindset to everything we do.</p><br><strong>What you'll be doing:</strong><br><div>
<p>Insify is looking for an entrepreneurial and analytical <strong>Product Manager </strong>to drive the growth and evolution of our <strong>Property &amp; Casualty (P&amp;C) portfolio</strong>. This role focuses on the essential "bread and butter" products for SMEs: including General Liability, Professional Indemnity, and Property insurance.</p>
<p>Unlike traditional PM roles, you won't just be managing features; you will be the "CEO" of your products. You will bridge the gap between complex insurance logic and a seamless digital user experience. You use your deep understanding of our customers and data native approach to translate technical policy wordings and insurance products into automated underwriting flows and digital-first customer journeys taking away the complexity for our customers.</p>
<p>This is a perfect role for someone with a background in business operations, consulting, or insurance who wants to move into a high-growth tech environment and take tangible ownership of a product's performance.</p>
</div><br><strong>What you’ll be up to (some examples):</strong><br>
<li><strong>Drive Product Strategy: </strong>Manage the roadmap for your products, ensuring they remain competitive, compliant, and easy to purchase online.</li>
<li><strong>Optimize the Funnel:</strong> Use data to identify friction points in the application process and work with Design and Tech to improve conversion rates.</li>
<li><strong>Scale New Markets:</strong> Support the launch of our digital proposition into new European markets, adapting local requirements into our scalable core platform.</li>
<li><strong>Stakeholder Management: </strong>Coordinate between Insurance, Tech, Marketing, and Customer Ops to ensure a unified product vision and smooth execution.</li>
<li><strong>Monitor Performance: </strong>Track loss ratios, retention, and customer feedback to iterate on the product and pricing strategy.</li>

<div>This role is a strong fit if you are a "doer" who loves to solve puzzles. You can dive deep into the fine print of an insurance policy one hour and brainstorm a new UI flow with a developer the next.</div><br><strong>Specifically, you bring:</strong><br><div>

<li><strong>2–4 years of experience</strong> in a high-growth startup or strategy consulting (Insurance, Fintech, or E-commerce preferred).</li>
<li><strong>Analytical Rigor:</strong> You are comfortable with Excel/data tools and use metrics to back up your decisions.</li>
<li><strong>Product Curiosity:</strong> You don't need to be a coder, but you should be excited about how APIs, automated underwriting, and LLMs can transform insurance.</li>
<li><strong>Bias for Action:</strong> You prefer "shipping and iterating" over "analyzing and waiting."</li>
<li><strong>Communication:</strong> Excellent English skills (Dutch, German, or French is a major plus given our European footprint).</li>
<li><strong>Educational Background:</strong> A degree in Business, Economics, Engineering, or a related field.</li>

</div><br><strong>Who this is not for:</strong><br>
<li><strong>You prioritize a 40-hour work week</strong>: We operate in a high-intensity 'startup-plus' environment. This isn't a standard 9-to-5; driving global impact here requires a level of dedication and 'always-on' spirit that goes well beyond the typical 40-hour work week.</li>
<li><strong>You prefer your comfort zone</strong>: We operate at the edge of our capabilities; if you aren't comfortable with constant change and being challenged, you won’t thrive here.</li>
<li><strong>You prefer to stay high-level</strong>: While this is a strategic role, no task is too small. If you aren't willing to roll up your sleeves and get into the "weeds" of execution, this isn't the right fit.</li>
<li><strong>A steep learning curve feels daunting</strong>: We move fast and use cutting-edge AI; you need to be an aggressive self-learner who can master new domains in days, not months.</li>
<br><strong>What we offer:</strong><br>
<li><strong>Competitive compensation</strong> - we want to attract and retain the best so we are offering a compensation package that aligns with that.</li>
<li><strong>In-office </strong>- come join us in our HQ in the center of Amsterdam.</li>
<li><strong>Grow in a growing company</strong> - there’s no better place to develop your talents and learn new skills. Help us show the world that insurance can be simple, transparent and trustworthy.</li>
<li><strong>Experienced entrepreneurs</strong> - work with experienced and dedicated entrepreneurs as part of an international team.</li>
<li><strong>Energetic environment</strong> - as a start-up, we’re different from your usual insurers. We scale rapidly and you can pick your own initiatives, helping us grow as we help more and more customers across Europe.</li>
<br><strong>Our culture (read this carefully)</strong><br><div>
<p>We’re not just building a company, we’re building a&nbsp;<strong>category leader</strong>. That comes with ambition, responsibility, and pace.</p>
<p>Our culture is defined by three things:</p>

<li><strong>High ownership</strong><strong><br></strong>People own problems end-to-end. If something is unclear or broken, we don’t wait - we step in and fix it.</li>
<li><strong>High pace</strong><strong><br></strong>Priorities shift, and decisions are made quickly. We value momentum and learning over perfection.</li>
<li><strong>High standards</strong><strong><br></strong> Outcomes matter more than optics. We care about results, quality, and follow-through.<br><br></li>

<p>At the same time, <strong>you won’t be doing this alone</strong>.</p>
<p>We believe great work happens through <strong>close collaboration</strong>. We work in-person, challenge each other’s ideas, and expect contributions from everywhere, regardless of title or tenure. The best ideas often come from unexpected places, and we create space for them to surface.</p>
<p>This is a <strong>human-sized company</strong>. You’ll know the people you work with, you’ll be able to walk over to anyone to ask a question or test an idea, and you’ll be part of the day-to-day energy of building together:&nbsp; from whiteboard discussions to shared lunches, dogs in the office, and moments to pause and reset.</p>
<p>We hire smart, ambitious people who think like owners, value intellectual honesty, and are motivated by impact rather than comfort. If you enjoy challenge, responsibility, and building something meaningful <em>with</em> others, you’ll likely thrive here.</p>
<p>If you’re looking for predictability, narrow scopes, or a guaranteed 9-to-5, this likely won’t be the right fit - and that’s okay. We’d rather be honest upfront.</p>
</div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/insify/product-manager-insurance-pc-amsterdam-124103","tags":["Insurance"],"job_types":["Full-time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795134417},{"slug":"advance-pricing-analytics-actuary-amsterdam-333495","company_name":"Insify","title":"Advance Pricing Analytics Actuary","description":"<div><span style="font-size: 24px">About Insify</span></div><div><br></div><div><span style="font-size: 11pt">We are a start-up offering an end-to-end digital insurance platform focussing solely on European entrepreneurs and SMEs. We offer the best insurance to our customers thanks to our focus on user experience, our leading underwriting services, and our expertise in data. In short, we’ve made getting insured quick, transparent and simple.</span></div><div><br></div><div><span style="font-size: 11pt">We know how to innovate - our team of seasoned entrepreneurs has built a host of successful businesses in fintech and e-commerce (HelloFresh, Bloomon and SumUp to name a few!).We’ve already raised over €25M in funding from leading investors (Accel Ventures, Frontline Ventures, Visionaries Club, Nico Rosberg, etc.), who love what we do and see the potential for a revolution in digital insurance.</span></div><div><br></div><div><span style="font-size: 11pt">We started our journey in the Netherlands and with our mission to make business insurance fast, simple and fair we have been able to have a significant impact on that market. Since last year we also serve customers in France and Germany, and are rapidly expanding across the rest of Europe!</span></div><div><br></div><div><span style="font-size: 24px">How we work</span></div><div><br></div><div>At Insify, we’re building more than just an insurance company—we’re creating a culture that’s bold, caring, and built to make a real difference. Everything we do is driven by our core values:&nbsp;<b>grit</b>,&nbsp;<b>impact</b>,&nbsp;<b>care</b>, and&nbsp;<b>entrepreneurship</b>. </div><div><br></div><div>We show up with passion and perseverance. We solve real problems and put people first—especially our customers. And we’re always looking for smarter, faster, more human ways to do things. </div><div><br></div><div>That’s also why we’ve chosen a&nbsp;pro-office approach. We believe that working together, face to face, sparks creativity, builds stronger teams, and helps us learn faster—especially for new joiners. From spontaneous brainstorms to shared lunches, being in the same space makes the magic happen.</div><div><br></div><div>Joining Insify means being part of a team that truly backs each other and the entrepreneurs we serve. If you’re ready to grow, innovate, and help reshape the insurance industry from the inside out—we’d love to meet you.</div><div><br></div><div><span style="font-size: 24px">Insurance Team</span></div><div><br></div><div>We’re the team making insurance work for everyone and everything. At Insify, our Insurance crew is all about making sure the right coverages are available, affordable, and actually make sense for today’s entrepreneurs. We’re the bridge between customer needs and carrier capabilities—constantly exploring, negotiating, and building better insurance solutions. </div><div><br></div><div>From partnering with top carriers to developing our own products, we ensure our platform delivers complete, seamless coverage. Whether it’s a roofer in Rotterdam or a freelance designer in Berlin, we’re here to make sure no one’s left out. Our team includes insurance pros, actuaries, and product ops experts working hand-in-hand with product, legal, and compliance to reshape insurance from the inside out.</div><div><br></div><div><span style="font-size: 24px;">About the Role</span></div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>This is your chance to work in a<strong>&nbsp;dynamic company&nbsp;</strong>where innovation and precision go hand in hand to disrupt the insurance industry. You'll be part of our&nbsp;<strong>Insurance&nbsp;</strong>team, as lead to ensure the scalability and sustainability of our portfolio optimizing both the bottom and top lines.</div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
<div>We are a data-driven company and we don’t lose time on tasks with little to no value therefore, on top of modeling the risk, price elasticity, customer lifetime value, and other key business drivers and trends, you will also be supporting the full End-to-end automation, set up of proper data flows, tooling and overall pricing platform solution.</div><br><strong>What you will be doing</strong><br>
<li><strong>Pricing and Underwriting:</strong>&nbsp;Develop and refine pricing models, ensuring accurate underwriting and profitability while optimizing for growth.</li>
<li>Dig for and leverage&nbsp;<strong>internal and external data</strong>&nbsp;to develop predictive models that enhance pricing strategies and improve portfolio performance.</li>
<li>Evaluate and propose&nbsp;<strong>new ideas</strong>&nbsp;and collaborate with the team to develop and push in production innovative solutions (pricing elasticity and optimisation, behaviour and fraud scoring, exposure-based dynamic pricing…),&nbsp;</li>
<li>Work with&nbsp;<strong>internal stakeholders to integrate actuarial insights</strong>&nbsp;into product, tech, regulatory compliance, and overall company strategy.</li>
<li>Follow market trends to recommend adjustments to pricing and products.</li>
<li><strong>Lead&nbsp;</strong>relationships with risk carriers to drive impactful results.</li>
<li>Be part, with the pricing team, of the development of our End-to-end, fully automated,&nbsp;<strong>pricing and analytics platform</strong>&nbsp;leveraging on data and innovative in-house proprietary solutions to scale in a sustainable and efficient way and always stay ahead of competition.</li>
<br><strong>What you'll need</strong><br>
<li>Actuarial diploma (or equivalent).</li>
<li>2–3+ years of experience in&nbsp;<strong>pricing</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>underwriting</strong>&nbsp;within&nbsp;<strong>Property &amp; Casualty</strong>&nbsp;insurance or&nbsp;<strong>Life&nbsp;</strong>Insurance.</li>
<li>Strong&nbsp;<strong>data analytics</strong>&nbsp;skills and a passion for leveraging data to drive innovation.</li>
<li>A&nbsp;<strong>global mindset</strong>&nbsp;with exposure to developed insurance markets (e.g., UK, Germany, France) with a desire to disrupt a slow-moving industry.</li>
<li>Excellent analytical and<strong>&nbsp;problem-solving</strong>&nbsp;abilities with a desire to build new things.</li>
<li>Strong interpersonal skills—smooth&nbsp;<strong>communication&nbsp;</strong>and collaboration are key!</li>
<li><strong>Fluent in English</strong></li>
<br><strong>Bonus points if you:</strong><br>
<li>Have experience with both risk and commercial price modeling. +2 points if you also have experience with survival models.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Master in Python and/or R and/or SQL</li>
<div><span style="font-size: 24px;">What we offer</span></div><div><br></div><div><b>Competitive compensation</b>&nbsp;- we want to attract and retain the best so we are offering a compensation package that aligns with that.</div><div><b>Pension plan</b>&nbsp;- participation to Insify’s Pension Plan, with 6% employer contribution.</div><div><b>Travel reimbursement</b>&nbsp;- we help travelers with their commute.</div><div><b>Hybrid</b>&nbsp;- Possibility to work from home two times a week.</div><div><b>25 holidays days per year</b>&nbsp;- (+ extra day on Christmas eve if it’s a weekday!)</div><div><b>Subscription to Alleo</b>&nbsp;- 50 EUR (net) monthly (cumulable) budget to spend on what you like - anything from gym memberships to UberEats!</div><div><b>Company events&nbsp;</b>- Monthly team drinks, quarterly offsites, lunch and learns, parties, merch and FUN!</div><div><b>Company Macbook</b>&nbsp;- get the best laptop to get your job done in no time!</div><div><b>Quickly develop your career</b>&nbsp;- there’s no better place to develop. We are growing and you can grow with us! Inhouse leadership programs and coaching</div><div><b>High degree of autonomy</b>&nbsp;- it’s time to ACTUALLY make an impact!</div><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/insify/advance-pricing-analytics-actuary-amsterdam-333495","tags":["Insurance"],"job_types":["Full-time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795134417},{"slug":"staff-software-engineer-os-integration-491586","company_name":"mozilla","title":"Staff Software Engineer, OS Integration","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;gmail_default&quot; style=&quot;font-size: small;&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Mozilla?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Mozilla Corporation is the non-profit-backed technology company that has shaped the internet for the better over the last 25 years. We make pioneering brands like Firefox, the privacy-minded web browser. Now, with more than 225 million people around the world using our products each month, we’re shaping the next 25 years of technology and helping to reclaim an internet built for people, not companies. Our work focuses on diverse areas including AI, social media, security and more. And we’re doing this while never losing our focus on our core mission – to make the internet better for people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The Mozilla Corporation is wholly owned by the non-profit 501(c) Mozilla Foundation. This means we aren’t beholden to any shareholders — only to our mission. Along with thousands of volunteer contributors and collaborators all over the world, Mozillians design, build and distribute &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;open-source&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; software that enables people to enjoy the internet on their terms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the OS Integration team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The OS Integration team ensures Firefox works well with the host operating system and environment. We’re a distributed team with expertise in Windows, macOS, and Linux-based operating systems. Our responsibilities include developing fixes and improvements for Firefox related to Windows, macOS, and Linux environments. This might include integration with a new OS feature or fixing an OS-specific user interface bug. Other responsibilities include native crash reporting, OS abstraction layers, sandboxing, hardening, installer, updater, device APIs, and enterprise DLP support.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;As a member of the OS Integration team, you’ll develop fixes, improvements, and new features for Firefox. The role will lean on your Windows expertise, but projects may have a cross-platform component. This role will include development of features for Firefox in enterprise environments especially implementation of Data Loss Prevention (DLP) features. As a Staff Software Engineer, you’re a clear communicator and expert in your domain, ready to work on multi-month projects. You’ll contribute to the team through code review, mentoring, and discussion.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
