 innovation at the forefront of sustainable aviation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Life Cycle Assessment: </strong>Build a framework to assess life cycle performance of various innovative SAF production routes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>GHG reduction calculation</strong>: Calculate the GHG reduction potential of selected SAF production routes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Policy Fit</strong>: asses the fit of selected SAF production routes with European SAF policy such as REFUELEU Aviation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team collaboration:</strong> Work closely with external partners, contributing findings, insights and ideas to ongoing research and development activities.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Your profile</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">You recognize yourself in the following:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Master’s student with a background in science or engineering (enrolled for the full duration of the internship)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong interest in renewable fuels, energy transition or sustainable technologies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience or academic exposure with Life Cycle Analysis and GHG reduction calculations is a must. Able to work independently, strong analytical skillset and a structured approach to complex technical questions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working with Excel, Word and PowerPoint</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in English, both written and spoken</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full-time availability for a 6-month internship starting 15th of February 2027</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>About SkyNRG</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since 2009, SkyNRG has been a change maker in the aviation industry. We are dedicated to supplying and producing high-integrity Sustainable Aviation Fuel (SAF), making sustainable aviation a reality.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaboration is fundamental to achieving our ambition. We nurture genuine relationships with global partners in our drive to make SAF <em>the</em> alternative to fossil jet fuel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our in-house team of SAF experts have helped over 60 airlines and corporates reduce their climate impact using the Book &amp; Claim mechanism; the most transparent and traceable way to support aviation sustainability with real emission reductions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sustainability is woven into the fabric of our company. We maintain an independent Sustainability Board, which advises the company on feedstocks and provides strategic guidance on wide-ranging sustainability issues. SkyNRG operations are certified against the RSB EU RED, CORSIA, and Book &amp; Claim standards.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At SkyNRG, you’ll find:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An innovation-driven culture – where big ideas turn into real impact</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growth opportunities – in a fast-scaling, industry-changing company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative team – where your ideas and expertise are valued</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A mission that matters – leading the change in the energy transition by producing and supplying high-integrity SAF</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What we offer</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a brand-new office in the heart of Amsterdam, designed for collaboration and creativity. Most importantly, you’ll have the opportunity to contribute to a truly game-changing green initiative, making a real impact on the aviation industry and the planet.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Besides that,