description":"<h3>WHO WE ARE 🌍</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Creating content that resonates is great — turning that attention into growth is even better. That's what Manychat does.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our AI-powered automations help creators and brands engage with audiences across Instagram, Messenger, WhatsApp, and TikTok — at the right moment, with the right message, minus the manual work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're 400+ people across three continents behind the leading platform for conversational growth, with AI skills shaping how we build, how we work, and how we grow.</p><h2>WHO WE'RE LOOKING FOR 🌟</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Want to own how the backend works for everyone, not just one corner of it?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a Senior Backend Engineer who works across PHP and Python and wants a say in the bigger picture. You’ll lead company-level projects like our Auth Service: one authorization layer for PHP and Python, so Python products can handle their traffic directly instead of going through PHP. When things are unclear, you’ll research first, weigh the trade-offs and write them down. Then you’ll ship in small, safe steps. You’ll also decide where code should live based on what’s best for the system, not on which language you know best.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product teams will come to you for advice, reviews, and a way through when they're stuck. The team is still taking shape, so you'll also help define ownership, standards, and how we work. If that mix of deep technical work and influence across teams sounds like you, keep reading.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>YOUR FUTURE TEAMMATES 👋</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Meet the Backend Platform team:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're a small team of engineers from core PHP, Infra, and AI backgrounds. We lead technical initiatives across the whole backend and own its health. Product teams build and run their own components, and we give them the tools, standards, and expertise to do it well. Each of us leads our own project, from planning to agreeing with other teams to production. We work in weekly cycles and write our decisions down. Right now we're bringing PHP and Python platform work together into one common backend platform.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>WHAT YOU'LL DO 🚀</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead company-level technical projects end to end, from design and planning to rollout and support, such as completing our Auth Service development and shaping authorization as a separate layer for PHP and Python.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape the shared PHP and Python platform, and decide where each module should live based on the needs of the whole system.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the foundations that let new Python products launch and scale without being wired through PHP each time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define clear ownership of technical components across the backend, including who owns monitoring and knowledge for each.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve how we spot and handle problems: bug and incident management, less noise in alerts and error tracking, and Grafana Cloud dashboards for how services interact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Find root causes across PHP and Python services using metrics, logs, and distributed tracing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make performance part of everyday work, not something we fix after incidents: clear performance metrics, tools that show where things slow down, and analysis of unusual user behavior that causes degradation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make architecture decisions with high load in mind, working with databases, servers, proxies, and DNS alongside the Infra team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with the Security team to fix vulnerabilities, build in security practices, and keep libraries and dependencies up to date.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve developer experience: dev environment, CI/CD, routine automation, one documentation approach for PHP and Python, and tools for AI coding assistants.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn product teams' requests into solutions: find what really hurts, propose the best fix, and support them with architecture advice and reviews in shared components.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>TO SHINE IN THIS ROLE 💥</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You'll need:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Production backend experience in PHP or Python, and the ability to read and work with the other. You'll write production code in both.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with high-load production systems and improving their performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing multi-component systems with clear boundaries, planning for failures, rollout, and rollback, with security in mind.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience comparing technical options, naming the trade-offs, and explaining your choice in writing (ADRs, Design Docs).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on observability experience: metrics, dashboards, alerts, logs, and distributed tracing, and using them to find root causes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading a project that spans several teams: breaking it into small, testable steps, getting other teams on board, and taking it to production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of improving engineering quality beyond your own tasks, for example setting up error monitoring, or a new process when things kept breaking.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enough infrastructure knowledge (databases, servers, proxies, DNS) to work well with Infra and see how your changes affect them.</p></li><li><p style="mi