u will lead Backend, Frontend, Full Stack and QA engineers building the platforms that help patients find their treatment options.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Expanded Access Program (EAP) platform and Clinical Trials (CT) platform connect patients and healthcare professionals with treatments in development and give our BioPharma Partners the tools to run their programs and trials. You’ll shape how these platforms grow, building a high-performing team that ships well-designed, scalable, secure and compliant software, and delivers it on time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You won’t do it alone. You’ll partner closely with Product, Design, EAP and CT Operations, and our Platform colleagues in DevOps, Security and Data. Together, you’ll turn ambitious company goals into product outcomes that make a real difference in patients’ lives.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Given that most of our team is located in the Netherlands, we only consider candidates for this position who live within commuting distance of our office in Amsterdam.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll do in this role:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead, mentor and manage a team of Backend, Frontend, Full Stack and QA engineers. Foster a collaborative, inclusive and high-performing culture.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own engineering delivery for your areas of the EAP and CT platforms, from discovery through to release and operation in production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Product Managers and Designers to shape the roadmap, refine priorities, and plan and execute features and improvements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Provide technical leadership in architecture and design, ensuring solutions are robust, maintainable, scalable and secure. Work with engineers on decisions about tools, frameworks and approaches.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Champion engineering best practices: proactive exploration AI-enabled and agentic development, code quality, testing, code review, API design, observability, documentation and secure development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure quality and compliance requirements are built into how the team works. This includes data privacy and the regulatory context of healthcare.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a culture of ownership, experimentation and continuous improvement, including healthy team rituals and retrospectives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Recruitment to attract, hire and onboard top talent.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you bring to the table:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">6+ years of experience in software engineering, with a solid background in backend, frontend or full stack development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of experience leading or managing engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proven track record of delivering high-quality web products and developing engineers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on familiarity with modern backend and frontend technologies. Experience with Python and Angular is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong understanding of Agile ways of working, product development and engineering best practices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication skills, with the ability to work cross-functionally and influence stakeholders at all levels.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A passion for working in a mission-driven organisation focused on improving patient outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a regulated domain such as healthc