ounting leader on the ground as that footprint expands.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You will stand up and scale the accounting function while partnering with Legal, Tax, Treasury, Payroll, and Operations as each new jurisdiction comes online. This is a leadership seat: you will hire, develop, and lead the accounting team in Amsterdam, and manage the outsourced providers supporting the countries where we do not yet have our own people.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The ideal candidate has run a multi-country close, is fluent in the difference between a US GAAP reporting package and a local statutory filing, and would rather design the process than inherit it. Join us in our mission to disrupt the defense industry and elevate your career with a team dedicated to making a significant impact on a global scale.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the month-end, quarter-end, and year-end close for the Company’s legal entities across Continental Europe and the Middle East, delivering to internal deadlines while ensuring the accuracy of financial data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own statutory reporting across the region, including statutory financial statements, local reporting differences, and adherence to local filing deadlines in each jurisdiction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage local statutory audits end to end, acting as the primary point of contact for local auditors while coordinating with the HQ team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review journal entries, account reconciliations, and fluctuation analyses; validate foreign currency remeasurement and translation impacts for the region’s entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own accounts payable operations and the procure-to-pay cycle for the region, from invoice receipt through payment disbursement, including vendor relationship management and payment performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, develop, and lead the regional accounting team in Amsterdam - including accounting managers and specialists - as the Company grows throughout the region, and manage outsourced accounting providers where local work is performed externally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary accounting liaison between the US parent company and the&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the accounting workstream on new entity and country launches, partnering with Legal on incorporation and registration and with Business Operations on site readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure adherence to internal controls and accounting policies, and design and document new controls as entities and requirements come online.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Tax, Treasury, and Payroll on VAT and local tax filings, transfer pricing support, intercompany settlement, cash forecasting, and payroll approvals across the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the configuration and ongoing maintenance of the region’s legal entities within the Company’s ERP, including any local statutory reporting basis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and execute opportunities for process improvement, including the adoption of automation and AI tools, so that the function scales faster than its headcount.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with regional operational and program leaders to support business decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on ad-hoc projects with accounting and finance teams across the Company, from leases and fixed assets to inventory, intercompany, and tax provision support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;WHO YOU ARE:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of progressive accounting experience, including 5+ years in a supervisory or management role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning the close and statutory deliverables for multiple legal entities in more than one country.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading an accounting team across more than one country, including the development of other managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working within a global organization reporting to a US parent; public accounting experience a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RA, ACA, ACCA, CPA, or equivalent certification preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of US GAAP and IFRS, with practical experience in local statutory reporting requirements across European jurisdictions; Middle East exposure a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing local statutory audits and external accounting or audit providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel skills and proficiency with ERP systems (Oracle Fusion Cloud preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent leadership, team management, and interpersonal skills, with a track record of hiring and developing accountants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and project management skills, with the ability to keep multiple jurisdictions and workstreams on schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable building process where little exists today, with a proven ability to manage competing priorities in a high growth organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with a mindset for continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to work effectively with colleagues across time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English; additional European languages a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The salary range for this role is an estimate based on a wide range of compensation factors, inclusive of base salary only. Actual salary offer may vary based on (but not limited to) work experience, education and/or training, critical skills, and/or business considerations. Highly competitive equity grants are included in the majority of full time offers; and are considered part of Anduril&#39;s total compensation package. Additionally, Anduril offers top-tier benefits for full-time employees, including:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;At Anduril, we invest in our people. Our comprehensive, competitive benefits package (available at little to no cost to employees) ensures you’re supported in health, recovery, and whatever comes next.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;For more information, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.anduril.com/careers&quot;&gt;Explore Our Benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;RichText column1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Protecting Yourself from Recruitment Scams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;Anduril is committed to maintaining the integrity of our Talent acquisition process and the security of our candidates. We&#39;ve observed a rise in sophisticated phishing and fraudulent schemes where individuals impersonate Anduril representatives, luring job seekers with false interviews or job offers. These scammers often attempt to extract payment or sensitive personal information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;RichText column2&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;To ensure your safety and help you navigate your job search with confidence, please keep the following critical points in mind:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No Financial Requests:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Anduril will never solicit payment or demand personal financial details (such as banking information, credit card numbers, or social security numbers) at any stage of our hiring process. Our legitimate recruitment is entirely free for candidates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please always verify communications:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct from Anduril: If you receive an email from one of our recruiters, it will &lt;em&gt;only&lt;/em&gt; come from an ----- address.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Via Agency Partner: If contacted by a recruiting agency for an Anduril role, their email will clearly identify their agency. If you suspect any suspicious activity, please verify the agency&#39;s authenticity by reaching out to &lt;a ----------
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exercise Caution with Unsolicited Outreach:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;If you receive any communication that appears suspicious, contains grammatical errors, or makes unusual requests, do not engage. Always confirm the sender&#39;s email domain is ----- before providing any personal information or clicking on links.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;detailElios&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What to Do If You Suspect Fraud:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Should you encounter any questionable or fraudulent outreach claiming to be from Anduril, please report it immediately to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a ---------- Your proactive caution is invaluable in protecting your personal information and upholding the security and trustworthiness of our recruitment efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Privacy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;To view Anduril&#39;s candidate data privacy policy, please visit &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/&quot;&gt;https://anduril.com/applicant-privacy-notice/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;335551550&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335551620&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;By submitting your application, you consent to Anduril Industries using a third-party service provider to conduct pre-employment risk, integrity, and due diligence screening and assessing potential risks as part of your application process. This third-party service provider provides risk-intelligence services that may include analysis of sanctions and watchlists, adverse media, public-record information, and other lawful open-source or commercial data sources. This third-party service provider does not act as a consumer reporting agency. Use of this provider helps to ensure compliance with applicable laws and protect technology, intellectual property, and organizational security.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/andurilindustries/senior-international-accounting-manager-amsterdam-255619","tags":["Finance & Accounting : Accounting : Accounting"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795103728},{"slug":"account-executive-amsterdam-336577","company_name":"Red Gate","title":"Account Executive","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>At a glance</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location: </strong>Amsterdam</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In-office expectation: </strong>At least twice a week</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Employment type: </strong>Permanent, 40 hours per week, Monday to Friday</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Salary: </strong>52000 – 75000 EURO Base plus Commission (50/50 Split)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why this role exists: </strong>To grow Redgate's presence with mid-market companies across Benelux and the Nordics, helping more organisations manage their data and databases with confidence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Redgate</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Redgate brings together people who want to do their best work in an environment built on trust, accountability, and collaboration.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We build solutions that help data professionals securely manage the data and databases that their organizations depend on, a space that's only becoming more critical as systems scale, data regulations increase, and AI adoption accelerates.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI at Redgate</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">By 2028, Redgate will operate as an expert-plus-agent company, with domain experts amplified by AI, delivering customer value at a pace our peers can't match.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI handles the heavy lifting. Our people control the judgement. Everyone at Redgate works with Claude, giving you access to the best AI tools from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why join our Northern Europe Sales team?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work in a team that cares about craft, collaboration, and quality.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">There's real scope to grow your skills and impact, with clear pathways and support.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We value sustainable delivery, with good ways of working and time to improve how we work.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll drive new sales of Redgate's solutions into mid-market companies across Benelux and the Nordics, based in our Amsterdam office and reporting to our Sales Director, Northern Europe. This is a quota-carrying role covering the whole sales cycle, from outbound prospecting and qualification through to evaluation, close and ongoing account care. You'll have real ownership of your territory and the judgement to decide where your time goes.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own your territory plan and pipeline, moving many opportunities forward at once and deciding where to focus to hit your goals</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with pre-sales engineers, project managers and marketing managers to win new business</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Become a trusted advisor to your customers, learning their key business challenges and staying accountable for the delivery of Redgate solutions</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Grow relationships with customer accounts of all sizes, long after the first deal closes</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Report on pipeline and forecast through our customer relationship management (CRM) system, keep an eye on the competition, and travel to customers when it helps win the deal</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What makes you a great fit</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of meeting or exceeding sales goals across a large territory, with experience building pipeline through outbound prospecting</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience running complex, non-transactional sales, including applying the MEDDPICC qualification framework</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong collaboration skills, working across pre-sales, project management and marketing, with the autonomy and judgement to make good decisions independently</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear, confident written and spoken communication with customers, colleagues and management</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A genuine interest in technology and the ability to keep accurate pipeline and forecasts in a CRM</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Salary range: </strong>52000 – 75000 EURO Base plus Commission (50/50 Split)</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid working home and Amsterdam office</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monthly wellbeing allowance and generous paid time off</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuine investment in learning, development, and career progression</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private health insurance</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">See our full list of benefits here: <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.red-gate.com/our-company/careers/benefits/"><u>Careers at Redgate, Benefits</u></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What happens next?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your application will be reviewed by a person. We don't use AI or automated tools to assess applications. Every profile is read by one of our Talent Partners.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll hear back within a few days. Whether it's a next step or a no, we aim to respond promptly so you're not left wondering.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our interview process is straightforward and consistent. You'll find more detail on our typical hiring process below, so you know what's coming and why.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Belonging at Redgate</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe that people do their best work in an environment built on respect, fairness, and trust, and that diverse perspectives lead to better outcomes. Redgate is an equal opportunity employer, and we make hiring decisions based on skill, potential, and alignment with our values.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can read more about how we approach belonging and inclusion at Redgate on our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.red-gate.com/our-company/careers/belonging/"><u>Belonging at Redgate page</u></a></p><hr><p>Compensation: €52K – €75K • Offers Commission</p><ul><li> • Base Salary €52K – €75K • Offers Commission</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/red-gate/account-executive-amsterdam-336577","tags":["Chief Revenue Officer"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795102816},{"slug":"internship-social-media-marketing-at-international-baby-and-kids-brand-start-feb-mar-27-weesp-375914","company_name":"Petite Amélie","title":"Internship - Social Media Marketing at International Baby- and Kids Brand (Start Feb / Mar 27)","description":"<p>Petite Amélie is a fast-growing brand, cherished by young parents and influencers across Europe. We design and produce beautiful children's furniture, accessories, and toys. Our webshops are available in the Netherlands, Belgium, France, Germany, and the UK, and we have three concept stores in these countries. Our office, where approximately 30 people work, is conveniently located next to the Weesp train station, just 15 minutes from Amsterdam.</p><p>We are excited to offer several internship opportunities within our international Marketing & E-commerce team. This team manages our webshops and marketing channels, including Google, Facebook, TikTok, and Instagram.</p><p>Content management is a crucial component of our marketing strategy, and as a brand with our own products, we have the ability to create stunning content. You can be a part of this exciting journey!</p><h2>Tasks</h2><p>We will involve you in many things. As social media intern, your main tasks can be:</p><ul><li><p>Create content (visuals, video and copy) for Instagram, Facebook, TikTok and Pinterest</p></li><li><p>Schedule & publish content</p></li><li><p>Create landing pages</p></li><li><p>Competitor and inspirational research</p></li><li><p>Help writing catchy texts with our training in SEO practices</p></li><li><p>Together with our social media expert, replying on messages and comments in our social media pages</p></li><li><p>Analyze results of social media posts</p></li><li><p>Community Management</p></li><li><p>Create Emails and Newsletters</p></li><li><p>learn all about CRM</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><p>Are you:</p><ul><li><p>Student (Creative business)</p></li><li><p>Living in Holland (or can relocate easily - this is a must)</p></li><li><p>You are fluent in English. (Also fluent in Dutch, French or German is beneficial)</p></li><li><p>Fulltime available</p></li><li><p>Proactive, curious and go-getter</p></li><li><p>A good eye for style, design and creativity</p></li><li><p>Excellent writing in the English language</p></li><li><p>Teamplayer</p></li></ul><p>… then we’d love to hear more about you!</p><h2>Benefits</h2><p>What we have to offer:</p><ul><li><p>A full-time internship of minimum 6 months</p></li><li><p>Be a real part of an enthusiastic and warm team</p></li><li><p>The opportunity to learn a lot</p></li><li><p>Great guidance from our team</p></li><li><p>Monthly compensation, refund of transportation costs and a laptop</p></li><li><p>FUN! We love to celebrate our success!</p></li></ul><p>Want to join? Please send us your resume and tell us a bit more about yourself. As content will be an important part of your task, we appreciate a story or reel to introduce yourself. We are looking forward to meeting you.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/petite-amelie/internship-social-media-marketing-at-international-baby-and-kids-brand-start-feb-mar-27-weesp-375914","tags":["Social Media Manager"],"job_types":["Internship","internship","no experience required / student"],"location":"Weesp","created_at":1795093300},{"slug":"senior-staff-site-reliability-engineer-server-infrastructure-amsterdam-304694","company_name":"Nebius","title":"Senior/Staff Site Reliability Engineer (Server Infrastructure)","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;amp;D.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;The Role&lt;/h3&gt;
Server Infrastructure is a Site Reliability Engineering (SRE) team responsible for the full lifecycle of Nebius Cloud hardware: from newly delivered bare metal through provisioning, operation, maintenance, and decommissioning. Almost every Nebius service runs on servers within our domain. Our mission is to make the hardware layer fast, reliable, and invisible.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We apply software engineering to infrastructure operations. We build services and automation that bring servers into the cloud, keep them healthy, recover them from failures, and retire them safely. Our work spans CPU and GPU platforms, the base GNU/Linux system, and the infrastructure supporting our hardware fleet.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;As a Senior / Staff Engineer, you’ll take ownership of complex infrastructure challenges and help shape the team’s technical direction. You’ll combine hands-on engineering with architecture, mentoring, and coordination across teams, turning operational needs into reliable services and automation.&lt;br&gt;You’ll work closely with data center engineers, capacity managers, cloud compute developers, networking teams, and hardware suppliers. Your work will directly affect the reliability and capacity of the entire cloud platform.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Y&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;our responsibilities will include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and operate services for netboot, provisioning, maintenance, automated recovery, and decommissioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical initiatives from problem definition and design through implementation and production operation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape the technical roadmap, balancing reliability improvements, new hardware integration, and long-term engineering work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define meaningful reliability indicators and service level objectives, using them to guide engineering priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce operational toil by turning recurring failures and manual procedures into reliable automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve on-call practices, incident response, and learning through blameless incident reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen fleet observability, alerting, testing, deployment safety, and operational readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive support for new CPU and GPU platforms and improvements to the base GNU/Linux system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers, provide thoughtful design and code reviews, and help the team develop sound engineering practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate delivery across teams, communicate technical tradeoffs, and resolve dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We expect you to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong software engineering experience in Go and a solid understanding of Linux systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing, building, and operating infrastructure services, including distributed systems and failure handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of owning complex technical initiatives and bringing them into production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical knowledge of SRE principles: service level objectives, observability, incident management, capacity planning, and toil reduction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound technical judgment and the ability to guide architecture and investigate difficult production problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring engineers and improving engineering practices through collaboration and technical example.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication and the ability to work effectively across engineering and operational teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;We welcome candidates at senior and staff levels. The scope of ownership and technical influence will reflect your experience.&lt;br&gt;Experience with hardware provisioning, &lt;strong&gt;bare metal infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;GPU platforms&lt;/strong&gt;, or large server fleets would be valuable.&lt;br&gt;Familiarity with &lt;strong&gt;Kubernetes, infrastructure as code, GitOps, SaltStack, and Terraform&lt;/strong&gt; is also useful.&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;We conduct coding interviews as part of the process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career growth and learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and innovative culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work on impactful AI projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International environment and talented teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s it like to work at Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fast moving&amp;nbsp;- Bold thinking&amp;nbsp;- Constant growth&amp;nbsp;- Meaningful impact&amp;nbsp;- Trust and real ownership&amp;nbsp;- Opportunity to shape the future of AI&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and diverse workplace and to providing equal employment opportunities in all aspects of employment. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), national origin, ancestry, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must be authorized to work in the country in which they apply and will be required to provide proof of employment eligibility as a condition of hire.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need accommodations during the application process, please let us know.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/nebius/senior-staff-site-reliability-engineer-server-infrastructure-amsterdam-304694","tags":["SRE"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795092919},{"slug":"senior-site-reliability-engineer-data-platform-amsterdam-176366","company_name":"Nebius","title":"Senior Site Reliability Engineer (Data Platform)","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;amp;D.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3 id=&quot;The-Role&quot; data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;913&quot;&gt;The Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;923&quot;&gt;We’re looking for a &lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Senior Site Reliability Engineer &lt;/strong&gt;to join the team building and operating &lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Nebius Data Platform &lt;/strong&gt;— a distributed storage and a processing platform that acts as the company’s “source of truth” and the backbone of many internal (and some external) products.&lt;br&gt;Nebius Data Platform is a &lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;single multi-tenant ecosystem based on YTsaurus&lt;/strong&gt; — instead of running separate HDFS/Kafka/HBase-style systems, we provide storage, compute, and analytics capabilities inside one platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;923&quot;&gt;We operate across data centers worldwide, running YTsaurus in dedicated Kubernetes clusters with Kubernetes operators and supporting services written primarily in Go. We maintain our own Nebius distribution, develop functionality across the core and platform services, and contribute upstream where it makes sense. This gives us the ability to take improvements from design through implementation to production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;923&quot;&gt;At scale today, this includes&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;~500 servers, ~20k CPU cores&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;~10 PB of compressed&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;data&lt;/strong&gt; in our largest production cluster, supporting workloads ranging from business-critical pipelines and financial transactions to large-scale ML/LLM training datasets and compute.&lt;br&gt;As an SRE, you’ll combine software engineering with production ownership: understand how the platform behaves, identify what limits its reliability and growth, and build lasting improvements alongside the developers and teams who use it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ak-ul&quot; data-indent-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2365&quot;&gt;Own and improve the reliability, performance, and capacity of our YTsaurus clusters, with particular attention to data durability and predictable behavior under load.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2535&quot;&gt;Develop services, Kubernetes automation, and operational tooling in Go to simplify cluster provisioning, upgrades, and maintenance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2670&quot;&gt;Improve monitoring, alerting, and diagnostic tools so we can detect problems early and understand their impact on users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2794&quot;&gt;Investigate failures across Linux, networking, Kubernetes, and distributed storage and compute. Participate in on-call, lead incident investigations, and turn findings into lasting fixes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2985&quot;&gt;Improve resource utilization and workload isolation as the platform grows and serves more teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3085&quot;&gt;Work with platform developers and users to make architectural decisions, deliver changes safely, and reduce repetitive operational work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3225&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;We expect you to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ak-ul&quot; data-indent-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3251&quot;&gt;Experience operating distributed, stateful systems in production and taking responsibility for their reliability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3368&quot;&gt;Strong Linux and networking fundamentals, including the ability to investigate resource bottlenecks and failures beyond the application layer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3514&quot;&gt;Practical Kubernetes experience: deploying, operating, and troubleshooting production workloads.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3614&quot;&gt;Strong programming skills and experience building maintainable software. We primarily use Go; experience in another language and a willingness to learn Go are welcome.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3785&quot;&gt;A systematic approach to troubleshooting, using evidence from logs, metrics, traces, and system behavior.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;3894&quot;&gt;The ability to drive improvements from problem identification through delivery, communicate trade-offs clearly, and collaborate with developers and platform users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4061&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;It will be an added bonus if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ak-ul&quot; data-indent-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4103&quot;&gt;Experience with Big Data systems (YTsaurus/Hadoop/Spark/ClickHouse/Kafka-like ecosystems).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4197&quot;&gt;Experience developing Kubernetes operators or controllers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4259&quot;&gt;Experience with performance analysis, capacity planning, or resource management in multi-tenant systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;4367&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;We conduct coding interviews as part of the process.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career growth and learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and innovative culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work on impactful AI projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International environment and talented teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s it like to work at Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fast moving&amp;nbsp;- Bold thinking&amp;nbsp;- Constant growth&amp;nbsp;- Meaningful impact&amp;nbsp;- Trust and real ownership&amp;nbsp;- Opportunity to shape the future of AI&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and diverse workplace and to providing equal employment opportunities in all aspects of employment. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), national origin, ancestry, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must be authorized to work in the country in which they apply and will be required to provide proof of employment eligibility as a condition of hire.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need accommodations during the application process, please let us know.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/nebius/senior-site-reliability-engineer-data-platform-amsterdam-176366","tags":["SRE"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1795092919},{"slug":"senior-product-marketing-manager-amsterdam-498787","company_name":"Optics11","title":"Senior Product Marketing Manager","description":"<p><span style="color:#000000">Optics11 is a fast-growing high-tech company based in Amsterdam, developing advanced fiber optic sensing solutions for the most demanding environments. Our technology detects the earliest signs of failure in critical assets – from high-voltage energy infrastructure to subsea and defense applications – and gives our customers precise, real-time data they can act on.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW90758248 BCX8">As <strong>Senior Product Marketing Manager</strong> you will build a deep understanding of the end-to-end solutions (hardware and software) across all of Underwater Security (our OptiBarrier and OptiArray product lines and our software platform), and of the markets and customers they serve. You turn that understanding into clear positioning, compelling value propositions and go-to-market plans that help our sales teams win.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW90758248 BCX8">Optics11 is in its scale-up phase, and product marketing in Underwater Security is starting from a basic level. You will build the product marketing function from the ground up: you set up the frameworks, processes and tools it needs, while delivering tangible commercial results along the way. You start as an individual contributor, with the opportunity to grow a small product marketing team over time.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW90758248 BCX8">You will be part of the Product team in Underwater Security and work closely with our solutions Product Managers for hardware and software, Sales, Business Development, Marketing, Application Engineering, Customer Projects and R&amp;D teams.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW90758248 BCX8">No two weeks will look the same. You might analyze a competitor’s new seabed monitoring system, sharpen the value proposition for an anti-submarine warfare (ASW) tender, work on the launch of a new software release, train the sales team on a new product narrative, or help prepare a customer demo for a tradeshow such as UDT or Euronaval. You will own how our products are positioned, launched and sold in the market, support pricing decisions, and make sure your market insights support Optics11 product decision making.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW90758248 BCX8">Within your first 6–12 months, you will have evolved the foundations of product marketing in Underwater Security: clearly defined target segments and buyer personas, a positioning and messaging framework per product line, a competitive intelligence baseline, a repeatable launch process and a first sales enablement toolkit. Your work will sharpen our market focus, improve our win rate and help Optics11 scale its solutions commercially in demanding, high-stakes markets.&nbsp;</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>Responsibilities:</h4><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW6754320 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW6754320 BCX8">Build the product marketing function by setting up the frameworks, processes, templates and tools for positioning, launches, competitive intelligence, sales enablement and product marketing analytics, tracking pipeline contribution and win rates, and scaling them as the organization grows.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW6754320 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW6754320 BCX8">Define target markets and commercialization plans by analyzing market size, trends, buying contexts and customer needs across mission profiles such as anti-submarine warfare (ASW), intelligence, surveillance and reconnaissance (ISR) and critical underwater infrastructure (CUI) protection, prioritizing segments and use cases with Product Management and Business Development, and defining go-to-market approaches, channels and partnerships per segment (e.g. with prime contractors and system integrators).</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW6754320 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW6754320 BCX8">Lead competitive intelligence and market monitoring by tracking competitors, technologies, programs and tenders, running win/loss analyses, and sharing actionable insights with Product Management to shape strategy, roadmap and business cases.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW6754320 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW6754320 BCX8">Own product positioning, messaging and value propositions by developing clear, differentiated propositions per product line and segment, and translating technical capabilities into operational and commercial value for defense partners and clients.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW6754320 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW6754320 BCX8">Support Product Management on pricing and packaging by providing market, competitor and customer insights for pricing decisions on products and end-to-end solutions, and aligning price positioning with Sales.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW6754320 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW6754320 BCX8">Plan and execute product launches by introducing a launch process scaled to the size of each release, coordinating launch readiness across Product, Sales and Support, and providing product messaging, content and launch input to the Marketing team.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW6754320 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW6754320 BCX8">Enable sales and ensure commercial readiness by creating sales narratives, pitch decks, battlecards, objection handling and training, preparing customer demos, collateral and tender input with Tech Sales &amp; Bid Management and Application Engineering, and supporting Sales, Business Development and Marketing in key opportunities, tenders and trade shows.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <h4>Requirements:</h4><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW64577901 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW64577901 BCX8">Master’s degree in marketing, business or engineering.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW64577901 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW64577901 BCX8">5+ years of experience in product marketing for technical B2B or B2G solutions, preferably combining hardware and software (platform) products in defense or another industrial high-tech / high-compliance environment with long, complex sales cycles such as tenders and partner-led sales.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW64577901 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW64577901 BCX8">Proven experience building product marketing from the ground up in a scale-up: hands-on, pragmatic and entrepreneurial, setting up processes, frameworks and tools with limited resources while delivering results.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW64577901 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW64577901 BCX8">Demonstrable experience in defining value propositions, positioning and go-to-market plans, and executing them through launches and sales enablement.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW64577901 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW64577901 BCX8">Ability to quickly understand complex technology and translate it into clear, credible customer value.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW64577901 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW64577901 BCX8">Strong cross-functional leadership and stakeholder management skills at operational and management level.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW64577901 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW64577901 BCX8">Excellent verbal and written communication skills in English, capable of presenting to technical, commercial and executive audiences.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW64577901 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW64577901 BCX8">Proficiency in CRM and marketing automation tools such as HubSpot, and in analytics for funnel and performance reporting.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW64577901 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW64577901 BCX8">Willingness to travel, including to customers and international trade shows; driver’s license B (or international equivalent).</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW64577901 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW64577901 BCX8">Ability to pass a background / security screening by the Dutch AIVD/MIVD, as you will be working with clients in the defense industry.</p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW64577901 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#0B2A4A">Nice to Have&nbsp;:</span></strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW64577901 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW64577901 BCX8">Experience in ASW, ISR or CUI-related defense technology markets, or with underwater acoustics, is a big plus.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW64577901 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW64577901 BCX8">Experience with defense procurement, tenders and export-controlled products.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW64577901 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW64577901 BCX8">Understanding of pricing and packaging for hardware, software and recurring-revenue (license or subscription) models.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW64577901 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW64577901 BCX8">Experience working with prime contractors and system integrators.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW64577901 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW64577901 BCX8">Proficiency in tools such as Jira Product Discovery, Confluence, Miro, PowerBI.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW64577901 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW64577901 BCX8">Proficiency in Dutch language is a plus</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Screening</strong></p><p>You will work with clients in the defense and security sectors. Obtaining a Certificate of No Objection issued by the AIVD, the Dutch General Intelligence and Security Service, is mandatory. This means you will need to undergo a security screening. We will explain the process and guide you through the applicable requirements.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/optics11/senior-product-marketing-manager-amsterdam-498787","tags":["Product Management"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1795091489},{"slug":"senior-product-manager-towed-array-solutions-amsterdam-381643","company_name":"Optics11","title":"Senior Product Manager (Towed Array Solutions)","description":"<p><span style="color:#000000">Optics11 is a fast-growing high-tech company based in Amsterdam, developing advanced fiber optic sensing systems for the most demanding environments. Our technology detects the earliest signs of failure in critical assets – from high-voltage energy infrastructure to subsea and defense applications – and gives our customers precise, real-time data they can act on.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW207693355 BCX8">As Senior Product Manager Towed Array Solutions you join our towed array product group as its second Product Manager, as we expand the team to keep pace with our current growth. You will initially focus on the Submarine and Special Warfare Support Vessel (SSV) domain, working closely with the Product Manager UxV, and build a deep understanding of the towed array systems and solutions we supply to our defense partners and clients, and of the anti-submarine warfare (ASW) and intelligence, surveillance and reconnaissance (ISR) missions they support.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW207693355 BCX8">You are responsible, from a product point of view, for bringing towed array solutions for your domain to market end to end from the in-water array to dry-end interrogator hardware, edge processing and integration on the host platform. You own the product strategy, roadmap and lifecycle for your domain within the shared towed array roadmap and shape the end-to-end solution together with the Product Manager UxV Solutions and the Senior Product Manager Software Solutions, who owns the software and platform capabilities that support it. You apply and further strengthen our product discovery and delivery ways of working for your domain.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW207693355 BCX8">You will be part of the Product team in Underwater Security and work closely with the Product Managers for UxV, Software, OptiBarrier and Deployment Solutions, Product Marketing, System Architecture, R&amp;D, Engineering, Data Science, Sales, Customer Projects and Application Engineering teams.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW207693355 BCX8">Within your first 6–12 months, you will have defined a clear, evidence-based SSV strategy and roadmap aligned with the overall towed array roadmap, assumed full Product ownership of SSV-related programs, and aligned hardware, software and commercial teams on the most important capabilities. Your work will expand our capacity to serve customers and programs in parallel, reduce uncertainty and strengthen investment decisions, helping Optics11 bring scalable, commercially strong solutions to customers operating in demanding, high-stakes defense environments.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4>Responsibilities:</h4><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW237110949 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW237110949 BCX8">Own the SSV domain strategy by defining the direction for towed array solutions in your domain, aligned with the overall towed array product group strategy, identifying customer problems and market opportunities, and balancing near-term opportunities with long-term company goals.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW237110949 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW237110949 BCX8">Lead customer and market discovery by developing a deep understanding of operational use cases, mission profiles and buying contexts, validating direction with navies, primes, partners and system integrators, and synthesizing feedback from trials and deployed systems.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW237110949 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW237110949 BCX8">Own the SSV roadmap and end-to-end solution definition within the shared towed array roadmap by defining the capabilities required to address validated needs, balancing improvements, new functionality and technology evolution, and aligning software and platform requirements with the Senior Product Manager Software.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW237110949 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW237110949 BCX8">Provide product design authority by ensuring hardware concepts, architecture choices and development decisions remain aligned with the Underwater Security product vision and strategy throughout the product lifecycle, together with System Architecture team.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW237110949 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW237110949 BCX8">Develop business cases and commercial input by defining success measures, commercial objectives and pricing for your domain, providing evidence for portfolio investment decisions, and working with Product Marketing on market insights, positioning, value propositions and launch readiness.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW237110949 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW237110949 BCX8">Bring solutions to market end to end by driving productization, defining qualification and certification requirements at product and solution level (with Systems Engineering and System Architects defining them at engineering level), integration on host platforms and market introduction, including service and through-life support concepts together with Customer Projects and Application Engineering.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW237110949 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW237110949 BCX8">Coordinate the product core team by working with Systems Engineering on requirements and feasibility, Product Ownership and Technical Project Managers on executable increments, and Project Management on customer integrations and delivery; align priorities, platform choices and shared components with the Product Manager UxV; and align Sales, Business Development, Customer Projects and Engineering around progress, quality and outcomes to ensure we deliver on our roadmap commitments.</p></li></ul> <br> <h4>Requirements:</h4><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221171104 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221171104 BCX8">Master’s degree in engineering (e.g. electrical, mechanical, physics or acoustics), product development or a related technical field.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221171104 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221171104 BCX8">5+ years of experience in hardware product management, with a proven track record of bringing hardware-based systems or end-to-end solutions to market in defense or another industrial high-tech / high-compliance environment.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221171104 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221171104 BCX8">Strong understanding of complex systems combining sensors, electronics and software, and of how hardware, edge processing and software platforms come together in one solution.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221171104 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221171104 BCX8">Experience with the full hardware lifecycle: from requirements and development through qualification, production and market introduction to through-life support and ILS.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221171104 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221171104 BCX8">In-depth knowledge of product management and strategy methodologies, with demonstrable experience in defining product strategy and creating complete business cases.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221171104 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221171104 BCX8">Strong cross-functional leadership and stakeholder management skills at operational and management level.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221171104 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221171104 BCX8">Critical thinking, adaptability and a problem-solving mindset to creatively address user and customer pain points.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221171104 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221171104 BCX8">Excellent verbal and written communication skills in English, capable of conveying product decisions and roadmaps to technical and non-technical stakeholders.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221171104 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221171104 BCX8">Willingness to travel, including to customers and sea trials; driver’s license B (or international equivalent).</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221171104 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221171104 BCX8">Ability to pass a background / security screening by the Dutch AIVD/MIVD, as you will be working with clients in the defense industry.</p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW221171104 BCX8"><strong><span style="color:#0B2A4A">Nice to Have&nbsp;:</span></strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221171104 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221171104 BCX8">Experience with sonar, towed arrays or underwater acoustics, ideally in ASW or ISR applications, is a big plus.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221171104 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221171104 BCX8">Experience with naval surface vessel programs, ideally submarine or special warfare support missions.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221171104 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221171104 BCX8">Experience with defense procurement, naval platform integration and export-controlled products.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221171104 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221171104 BCX8">Experience with fiber optic sensing technology.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221171104 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221171104 BCX8">Proficiency in tooling such as Jira / Jira Product Discovery, Confluence, BigPicture, JAMA Connect, Siemens Polarion, Miro and PowerBI.</p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle1 SCXW221171104 BCX8"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW221171104 BCX8">Proficiency in Dutch language is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Screening</strong></p><p>You will work with clients in the defense and security sectors. Obtaining a Certificate of No Objection issued by the AIVD, the Dutch General Intelligence and Security Service, is mandatory. This means you will need to undergo a security screening. We will explain the process and guide you through the applicable requirements.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/optics11/senior-product-manager-towed-array-solutions-amsterdam-381643","tags":["Product Management"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Amsterdam, Noord-Holland, Netherlands","created_at":1795091489},{"slug":"junior-account-executive-groningen-280698","company_name":"ChurchDesk","title":"Junior Account Executive","description":"<p><span style="color:#121317">We help churches develop. Behind every church are people who give their time and heart to their community, and we want to make their work easier. Our software brings administration and communication together in one platform, so there’s less time for paperwork and more time for people.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#121317">More than 10,000 churches across Europe work with ChurchDesk, and together with Hagru we’re now growing fast in the Netherlands. Our Groningen team is at the heart of that growth, and we’re looking for someone who wants to grow with it.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Is this you?</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"><br>You’ve just graduated or are about to, or you have your first work experience behind you. You love talking to people, you’re curious, and you want a job where you learn fast and see the results of your work. You don’t need years of sales experience. We’ll teach you how to sell. What we’re looking for is your energy, your curiosity and your drive to grow.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><span style="color:#121317">About your new role</span></h4><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Open doors:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You reach out to churches and congregations across the Netherlands that don’t use ChurchDesk or Hagru yet.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Start real conversations:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You learn about their daily work, their challenges and their plans, and show them how our platform can make life easier.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Own the process:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You guide churches from the first conversation all the way to signing, and you hand them over smoothly to onboarding.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Present with confidence:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You present ChurchDesk to church councils, staff and volunteers, online and in person.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Build relationships:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> You become a trusted partner in the Dutch church landscape and build relationships that last.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Learn every day:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> With training in consultative selling and your own coach, you’ll quickly develop into a confident sales professional.</span></p></li></ul> <br> <ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">A degree (or soon one) in any field, for example business, communication, theology or social sciences, or first work experience in a people-facing role.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">First sales or customer experience is a plus, for example from a student job, an internship or a study association, but it’s not a must.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You’re outgoing, enjoy talking to new people and don’t give up easily.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">You’re structured, take ownership and like working towards clear goals.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Fluent Dutch and good English, plus strong communication skills in conversations and in writing.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">A connection to church life, whether through your own church, volunteering or a student association, is a real plus.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>What We Offer</h3><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">A great start to your career:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Training in consultative selling and a dedicated coach who helps you grow.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Real responsibility from day one</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> in a growing international tech company.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Open feedback culture:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> We’re transparent, supportive and learn from each other.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">30 days of vacation</span></strong><span style="color:#121317">, because rest matters.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Trust and flexibility:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> We focus on results, not on counting hours, with a Scandinavian focus on balance.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Fancy a change of scenery?</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> Visit our offices in Copenhagen, Berlin or Oslo, with travel and expenses covered.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Unforgettable team experiences:</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> company events, sailing trips in Croatia, ski trips and visits to our Berlin office.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">A diverse team</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"> of different nationalities, ages and backgrounds, and a great office crew in Groningen.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Ready to start?</span></strong><span style="color:#121317"><br>Apply with your CV. A cover letter is optional, but we’d love to hear in a few lines why you want to start your career in sales with us. We look forward to meeting you!</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 style="text-align:start;"><strong>About ChurchDesk</strong></h3><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#000000">At ChurchDesk, we believe that the church plays an important role in society. Our platform is used by thousands of congregations to organise their work, improve communication with members, reach more people, and unlock new ways of fundraising.<br>Our customers are part of one of the largest and oldest institutions in the world: the Church. It is undergoing significant change to prepare for the future — and we are here to support that transformation. For churches across Europe, it is crucial to work more efficiently and stay connected to their members and communities.</span></p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#000000">ChurchDesk has been around for more than 15 years — evolving from a startup into an international company serving customers across Europe. And we’re just getting started!</span></p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#000000">We actively live our values in our daily work:</span></strong></p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#000000">#challenge:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> We challenge ourselves — and our customers — to continuously improve. We work like a professional sports team: with ambition, discipline, and strong team spirit.</span></p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#000000">#dogoodbusiness:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Doing good business is a marathon, not a sprint. It requires endurance, quality, and integrity — every single day.</span></p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#000000">#jointheride:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> The journey matters just as much as the destination. Be part of it, celebrate successes — and have fun! We value being together, especially in the office.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/churchdesk/junior-account-executive-groningen-280698","tags":["Revenue"],"job_types":["Entry","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Groningen, Groningen, Netherlands","created_at":1795091486},{"slug":"internship-dach-social-media-marketing-at-young-international-brand-jan-feb-27-weesp-144447","company_name":"Petite Amélie","title":"Internship DACH - Social Media & Marketing at International Baby- and Kids Brand (Jan / Feb 27)","description":"<p>Petite Amélie is a fast-growing and youthful brand, cherished by young parents and influencers across Europe. We design and produce beautiful children's furniture, accessories, and toys. Our webshops are available in the Netherlands, Belgium, France, Germany, and the UK, and we have three concept stores in these countries. Our office, where approximately 30 people work, is conveniently located next to the Weesp train station, just 15 minutes from Amsterdam.</p><p>We are excited to offer several internship opportunities within our international Marketing & E-commerce team. This team manages our webshops and marketing channels, including Google, Facebook, TikTok, and Instagram.</p><p>Content management is a crucial component of our marketing strategy, and as a brand with our own products, we have the ability to create stunning content. You can be a part of this exciting journey!</p><h2>Tasks</h2><p>We will involve you in many things. As social media intern, your main tasks can be:</p><ul><li><p>Create content (visuals, video and copy) for Instagram, Facebook, TikTok and Pinterest</p></li><li><p>Schedule & publish content</p></li><li><p>Create landing pages</p></li><li><p>Competitor and inspirational research</p></li><li><p>Help writing catchy texts with our training in SEO practices</p></li><li><p>Together with our social media expert, replying on messages and comments in our social media pages</p></li><li><p>Analyze results of social media posts</p></li><li><p>Community Management</p></li><li><p>Create Emails and Newsletters</p></li><li><p>learn all about CRM</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><p>Are you:</p><ul><li><p>Student (Creative business)</p></li><li><p>Living in Holland (or can relocate easily - this is a must)</p></li><li><p>You are fluent in German. (Also fluent in English is beneficial)</p></li><li><p>Fulltime available</p></li><li><p>Proactive, curious and go-getter</p></li><li><p>A good eye for style, design and creativity</p></li><li><p>Excellent writing in the German language</p></li><li><p>Teamplayer</p></li></ul><p>… then we’d love to hear more about you!</p><h2>Benefits</h2><p>What we have to offer:</p><ul><li><p>A full-time internship of minimum 6 months</p></li><li><p>Be a real part of an enthusiastic and warm team</p></li><li><p>The opportunity to learn a lot</p></li><li><p>Great guidance from our team</p></li><li><p>Monthly compensation, refund of transportation costs and a laptop</p></li><li><p>FUN! We love to celebrate our success!</p></li></ul><p>Want to join? Please send us your resume and tell us a bit more about yourself. As content will be an important part of your task, we appreciate a story or reel to introduce yourself. We are looking forward to meeting you.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/petite-amelie/internship-dach-social-media-marketing-at-young-international-brand-jan-feb-27-weesp-144447","tags":["Social Media Manager"],"job_types":["Internship","internship","no experience required / student"],"location":"Weesp","created_at":1795106848},{"slug":"stage-e-commerce-influencer-marketing-nl-be-fulltime-start-januari-februari-2027-weesp-124954","company_name":"Petite Amélie","title":"Stage E-commerce & Influencer Marketing (NL/BE), fulltime, start januari/februari 2027","description":"<p><strong>Wil je zien wat jouw ideeën doen voor een merk waar jonge ouders dol op zijn?</strong> Bij Petite Amélie zie je meteen het resultaat van je werk. Je zet bijvoorbeeld een samenwerking op met een Nederlandse influencer, of je bouwt een landingspagina voor een campagne, en je ziet direct wat het oplevert. Je haalt bij ons niet alleen koffie: vanaf dag één draai je volwaardig mee in ons marketing- & e-commerceteam, met de Nederlandse en Belgische markt als jouw terrein.</p><h3>Over Petite Amélie</h3><p>Wij ontwerpen en produceren meubels, accessoires en speelgoed voor baby- en kinderkamers, en jonge ouders in heel Europa zijn er dol op. We groeien snel, met webshops in Nederland, België, Frankrijk, Duitsland en het Verenigd Koninkrijk. Vanuit ons kantoor in Weesp (15 minuten met de trein vanaf Amsterdam Centraal) werken we met zo’n 30 collega’s aan het merk.</p><h3>Wat ga je doen?</h3><p>Ons team beheert de webshops en alle online kanalen. Organische groei en sterke content staan centraal. Je kiest samen met je begeleider waar je de nadruk op legt, op basis van je leerdoelen en interesses:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Influencers & samenwerkingen:</strong> je zoekt passende influencers en contentmakers in Nederland en België en neemt zelf contact met ze op. Je zet samenwerkingen op, zoals productgifting, contentdeals en campagnes, en je onderhoudt de relaties.</p></li><li><p><strong>Content & social:</strong> je maakt content voor Instagram, TikTok en Pinterest en doet community management.</p></li><li><p><strong>Campagnes & landingspagina’s:</strong> je helpt campagnes uitvoeren en bouwt en werkt aan pagina’s die converteren.</p></li><li><p><strong>Webshop & merchandising:</strong> je bepaalt mee hoe producten in de shop worden gepresenteerd.</p></li><li><p><strong>SEO & CRO:</strong> je zoekt uit waarom bezoekers wel of niet kopen, en wat we daaraan kunnen verbeteren.</p></li><li><p><strong>Data & onderzoek:</strong> je rapporteert over e-commerce-KPI’s en doet marktonderzoek naar nieuwe kansen.</p></li></ul><p>Aan het eind van je stage heb je echte resultaten en een eigen netwerk om te laten zien, en daarmee val je bij je volgende werkgever meteen op.</p><h3>Wie zoeken we?</h3><p><strong>Dit heb je echt nodig:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Je studeert bedrijfskunde, marketing, communicatie, economie of iets vergelijkbaars, op hbo- of wo-niveau, en je stage is onderdeel van je opleiding (met stageovereenkomst).</p></li><li><p>Je bent fulltime beschikbaar voor minimaal 6 maanden, vanaf januari of februari 2027.</p></li><li><p>Je woont in Nederland.</p></li><li><p>Je spreekt en schrijft vloeiend Nederlands, en je Engels is goed.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Dit maakt je een goede match:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Je pakt dingen zelf op, bent nieuwsgierig en denkt commercieel.</p></li><li><p>Je vindt het leuk om mensen te benaderen en relaties op te bouwen.</p></li><li><p>Je hebt oog voor design, interieur en esthetiek.</p></li><li><p>Je werkt nauwkeurig en graag samen.</p></li></ul><p>Herken je jezelf niet in elk punt? Solliciteer toch. Enthousiasme en leergierigheid wegen voor ons zwaar.</p><h2>Benefits</h2><p><strong>Dit bieden wij:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Een stagevergoeding van <strong>€650 per maand</strong></p></li><li><p>Een OV-reisproduct of reiskostenvergoeding, en een laptop van de zaak</p></li><li><p>Persoonlijke begeleiding van een vaste begeleider uit het team</p></li><li><p>Praktijkervaring in de hele e-commerce-mix: influencer marketing, social, community management, merchandising, webshopbeheer, analytics, SEO en CRO</p></li><li><p>Een warm, enthousiast team waarin je werk echt impact heeft, en waar we successen graag samen vieren</p></li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Klaar om ons te komen versterken?</strong></p><p>Stuur je CV en vertel ons kort wie je bent. Je kunt een motivatie schrijven, maar je mag jezelf ook voorstellen met een reel, story of een ander creatief format. Dat vinden we leuk, maar het is niet verplicht.</p><p><strong>Zo verloopt het:</strong> binnen een week hoor je van ons. Daarna volgt een (video)kennismaking met je toekomstige begeleider, en je hoort snel of je in januari of februari kunt starten.</p><p>Vragen? Neem contact op met Jasmijn van den Heuvel, Country manager E-com & marketing NL, via -----<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/petite-amelie/stage-e-commerce-influencer-marketing-nl-be-fulltime-start-januari-februari-2027-weesp-124954","tags":["Online Marketing"],"job_types":["Stage","internship","geen ervaring vereist / student"],"location":"Weesp","created_at":1795091457},{"slug":"remote-mobile-developer-utrecht-286555","company_name":"Luscii","title":"Mobile Developer","description":"<p>At Luscii, we develop several applications within the OMRON Digital Health Circle, including the Luscii Thuismeten app and OMRON Connect. Together, we build technology that makes healthcare more accessible, giving patients and healthcare professionals more space to focus on care. As a <strong>Mobile</strong> <strong>Developer</strong>, you will contribute to this mission by developing and improving the applications that connect people, devices and healthcare.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Our digital health solutions enable healthcare professionals to monitor patients remotely, helping people receive the right care in the right place. You will work across our mobile applications, creating reliable, intuitive and high-performing experiences for patients and healthcare professionals alike.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Beyond developing and improving our apps, you will help shape our technical direction, explore new technologies and share your expertise with colleagues. You will have the autonomy to take ownership, make technical decisions and contribute beyond your immediate responsibilities, supported by Luscii's Holacratic way of working.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>Your role</h3><p>As a Mobile Developer at Luscii, you will take ownership of the development, optimisation and maintenance of our mobile applications across iOS and Android. You bring ideas to life, make well-considered technical decisions and help ensure our applications remain performant, stable, scalable and easy to maintain.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>You will work closely with colleagues across development, QA and support, combining hands-on engineering with technical ownership. Whether you are building a new feature, exploring a technology through a proof of concept or resolving a production issue, you will help us continuously improve the quality and usability of our digital health solutions.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>What you will be doing:</p><ul><li><p>Develop, maintain and optimise mobile applications using native technologies such as Kotlin and Swift, with a focus on performance, stability and user experience.</p></li><li><p>Contribute to mobile architecture, technical design and modular codebases, applying clean architecture, object-oriented design principles and patterns such as MVVM and MVI.</p></li><li><p>Build intuitive user interfaces using technologies such as Jetpack Compose and SwiftUI, following platform-specific design guidelines.</p></li><li><p>Develop and maintain features that communicate with Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) devices, as well as web services, cloud platforms and APIs.</p></li><li><p>Build prototypes and proof of concepts to explore new technologies, validate technical approaches and identify opportunities for improvement.</p></li><li><p>Investigate and resolve production issues through debugging and performance analysis, covering areas such as memory management, multithreading and networking.</p></li><li><p>Contribute to code reviews, automated testing and CI/CD processes, sharing technical knowledge and helping colleagues make sound implementation decisions.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>Why Luscii?</h3><p><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://jobs.luscii.com/life-at-luscii/">Read more</a></u> about working at Luscii and <u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://jobs.luscii.com/how-we-work/">how</a></u> we work at Luscii/OMRON. Together, we are working on a mission to create space for care. Freedom, autonomy and ownership are of great importance in this. You are responsible for your own results and work according to the principles of Holacracy.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>Most important benefits</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Salary</strong>: € 4.600 - € 5.900 gross per month (based on 32 hours per week – that’s full-time at Luscii).</p></li><li><p><strong>Remote-first</strong>: Work from anywhere in The Netherlands. We stay connected through monthly in-person team days called <em>Assemblii</em>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Flexible setup</strong>: Create your own ideal workspace. Whatever works best for you - we’ve got you covered here.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>The ideal candidate…</h3><p>… probably doesn't exist, but if you can tick most of the checkboxes below, please apply! We are looking for somebody who is comfortable in taking ownership and making well-considered decisions independently. You enjoy the autonomy to shape your work and responsibilities, while actively seeking collaboration and alignment with others.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>You know when to step up, when to involve colleagues and when to move forward decisively. Working independently does not mean working in isolation for you. You feel at ease being both a self-starter and a committed team player, contributing to shared goals while taking responsibility for your own domain. You value open communication, transparency, and mutual trust.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p>You have at least five years of experience in mobile development, with a strong background in native Android and/or iOS development. You have extensive experience with Kotlin and/or Swift.</p></li><li><p>You have a relevant bachelor's degree, for example in Computer Science or Computer Engineering and you are familiar with working in an Agile environment.</p></li><li><p>You have a solid understanding of mobile architecture and soft